            "heading": "Part F: Saboot 4: Particles ek doosre ko aakarshan (attraction) se kheenchte hain",
            "headingHinglish": "Part F: Saboot 4: Particles ek doosre ko aakarshan (attraction) se kheenchte hain",
            "body": "Agar particles harkat karte rehte hain, to wo bikhar kyun nahi jaate? Lohe ki keel ke kan bikhar kyun nahi jaate? Kyunki particles ke beech ek **kheenchav (aakarshan)** hota hai jo unhe ek saath pakde rakhta hai. Ye kheenchav **kuch cheezon mein zyada** aur **kuch mein kam** hota hai.\n\n### Kheenchav ki taakat ek jaisi nahi hoti\n\nTeen cheezein lo: ek **lohe ki keel**, ek **chalk**, aur ek glass **paani**.\n\n| Cheez | Todna kaisa lagta hai | Matlab kheenchav |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Lohe ki keel** | Haath se todna lagbhag **namumkin** | Kheenchav bahut **zyada** |\n| **Chalk** | Haath se aasaani se toot jaata hai | Kheenchav **kam** |\n| **Paani** | Ungli se aasaani se alag kar do, bahta hai | Kheenchav aur bhi **kam** (par hai) |\n\n### Activity: Steel ka taar, chalk aur rubber band\n\n1. **Steel ka patla taar** (jaise cycle ka bahut patla ya tool-kit ka taar) lo aur use dono haathon se kheencho ya mod-mod kar todne ki koshish karo. Ye **mushkil se** tootega. (Zyada na kheencho, chot na lage.) Taar mein particles ka kheenchav **bahut zyada** hai.\n2. **Chalk** ka tukda lo aur use dono haathon se modkar todo. Wo **aasaani se** toot jaata hai. Kheenchav kam hai.\n3. **Rubber band** ko kheencho. Wo lambi hoti hai, aur chhodne par wapas aa jaati hai. Ye bhi kheenchav ki wajah se hota hai: particles ek doosre ko pakde rehte hain.\n\n### Paani ki boondein judti kyun hain?\n\nEk chikni plate par paani ki **do chhoti boondein** paas-paas rakho aur ek ko dheere se doosri ke paas le jaao. Dono **mil kar ek badi boond** ban jaati hain. Ye isliye hota hai kyunki paani ke particles ek doosre ko **kheenchte** hain.\n\n```\n   Pehle                    Judne ke baad\n\n    ( o o )   ( o o )          ( o o o o )\n    ( o o )   ( o o )          ( o o o o )\n\n   do alag boondein          ek badi boond\n```\n\n> **Figure 1.4** – Paani ki do chhoti boondein paas aane par particles ke aapas ke kheenchav ki wajah se ek badi boond bana leti hain.\n\nDhyan do: ye kheenchav (aakarshan) hi particles ko ek saath **pakde rakhta hai**, aur ye **cheez se cheez badalta hai**. Ye hi wajah hai ki koi cheez mazboot hai (loha), koi naram (rubber), aur koi bahne wali (paani). Is par aage ki classes mein aur detail aayegi; abhi sirf itna yaad rakho: **kheenchav hai, aur sab mein ek jaisa nahi**.",
