          {
            "heading": "Part G: Chaaron saboot ek saath",
            "headingHinglish": "Part G: Chaaron saboot ek saath",
            "body": "Ab Mr. Siddiqui ne Reshma se kaha: \"Ab tumhe agarbatti ka sawal solve karna hai. Batao, uski khushboo doosre kone tak kaise pahunchi?\"\n\nReshma ne socha aur boli: \"Sir, hawa matter hai, uske kan hain. Un kanon ke beech **jagah** hai, to agarbatti ke kan usme ghus sakte hain. Sab kan **harkat** karte rehte hain, isliye agarbatti ke kan phailte hain. Aur wo **bahut chhote** hain, isliye hume dikhte nahi, par naak se pata chal jaata hai.\"\n\nSir ne taali bajayi, \"Shabaash! Tumne teen saboot to ek hi sawal mein laga diye.\"\n\n| Saboot | Kya dikhata hai | Humari activity |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Particles **bahut chhote** hain | Dilution: 5 steps ke baad bhi rang |\n| 2 | Particles ke beech **jagah** hai | Cheeni ghulna, syringe |\n| 3 | Particles **harkat** karte hain | Agarbatti, ink, garam vs thanda |\n| 4 | Particles ek doosre ko **kheenchte** hain | Keel, chalk, paani ki boond |",
            "bodyHinglish": "Ab Mr. Siddiqui ne Reshma se kaha: \"Ab tumhe agarbatti ka sawal solve karna hai. Batao, uski khushboo doosre kone tak kaise pahunchi?\"\n\nReshma ne socha aur boli: \"Sir, hawa matter hai, uske kan hain. Un kanon ke beech **jagah** hai, to agarbatti ke kan usme ghus sakte hain. Sab kan **harkat** karte rehte hain, isliye agarbatti ke kan phailte hain. Aur wo **bahut chhote** hain, isliye hume dikhte nahi, par naak se pata chal jaata hai.\"\n\nSir ne taali bajayi, \"Shabaash! Tumne teen saboot to ek hi sawal mein laga diye.\"\n\n| Saboot | Kya dikhata hai | Humari activity |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Particles **bahut chhote** hain | Dilution: 5 steps ke baad bhi rang |\n| 2 | Particles ke beech **jagah** hai | Cheeni ghulna, syringe |\n| 3 | Particles **harkat** karte hain | Agarbatti, ink, garam vs thanda |\n| 4 | Particles ek doosre ko **kheenchte** hain | Keel, chalk, paani ki boond |"
          },
          {
            "heading": "Aam galtiyan (bachke rehna)",
            "headingHinglish": "Aam galtiyan (bachke rehna)",
            "body": "**Galti 1: \"Hawa matter nahi hai kyunki dikhti nahi.\"**\n\nNahi. Dikhna matter hone ki shart nahi hai. Hawa ka mass hai (gubbare wali activity) aur wo jagah gherti hai (ulte glass wali activity). Isliye hawa matter hai.\n\n**Galti 2: \"Roshni aur awaaz bhi matter hain.\"**\n\nNahi. Light, sound aur heat **energy** ke roop hain. Unka mass nahi hota aur wo jagah nahi gherti. Matter sirf wo hai jiska mass aur volume dono ho.\n\n**Galti 3: \"Cheeni paani mein ghulkar gayab ho jaati hai.\"**\n\nGayab nahi hoti. Wo chhote kanon mein tootkar paani ke kanon ke beech ki jagah mein chali jaati hai. Isliye paani meetha ho jaata hai (aur agar paani ko sukha lein to cheeni wapas mil jaati hai).\n\n**Galti 4: \"Diffusion tab hota hai jab hum hilaye-dulaye.\"**\n\nNahi. Diffusion apne aap hota hai, kanon ki apni harkat se. Hilane se mixing aur jaldi ho sakti hai, par diffusion ke liye hilana zaroori nahi hai.\n\n**Galti 5: \"Paani 'bhara hua' dikhta hai, isliye uske kanon ke beech koi jagah nahi hoti.\"**\n\nCheeni ka paani mein ghul jaana aur level ka lagbhag na badhna dikhata hai ki jagah hoti hai, bas wo bahut chhoti hai.\n\n**Galti 6: \"Dilution mein 10 guna ka matlab 10 mL paani milana hai.\"**\n\nDhyan do: 1 mL ghol ko 9 mL paani mein milane par **total 10 mL** hota hai, aur ghol **10 guna halka** hota hai. Agar 1 mL ghol mein 10 mL paani milaoge, to total 11 mL hoga aur ghol **11 guna** halka hoga, 10 guna nahi.",
            "bodyHinglish": "**Galti 1: \"Hawa matter nahi hai kyunki dikhti nahi.\"**\n\nNahi. Dikhna matter hone ki shart nahi hai. Hawa ka mass hai (gubbare wali activity) aur wo jagah gherti hai (ulte glass wali activity). Isliye hawa matter hai.\n\n**Galti 2: \"Roshni aur awaaz bhi matter hain.\"**\n\nNahi. Light, sound aur heat **energy** ke roop hain. Unka mass nahi hota aur wo jagah nahi gherti. Matter sirf wo hai jiska mass aur volume dono ho.\n\n**Galti 3: \"Cheeni paani mein ghulkar gayab ho jaati hai.\"**\n\nGayab nahi hoti. Wo chhote kanon mein tootkar paani ke kanon ke beech ki jagah mein chali jaati hai. Isliye paani meetha ho jaata hai (aur agar paani ko sukha lein to cheeni wapas mil jaati hai).\n\n**Galti 4: \"Diffusion tab hota hai jab hum hilaye-dulaye.\"**\n\nNahi. Diffusion apne aap hota hai, kanon ki apni harkat se. Hilane se mixing aur jaldi ho sakti hai, par diffusion ke liye hilana zaroori nahi hai.\n\n**Galti 5: \"Paani 'bhara hua' dikhta hai, isliye uske kanon ke beech koi jagah nahi hoti.\"**\n\nCheeni ka paani mein ghul jaana aur level ka lagbhag na badhna dikhata hai ki jagah hoti hai, bas wo bahut chhoti hai.\n\n**Galti 6: \"Dilution mein 10 guna ka matlab 10 mL paani milana hai.\"**\n\nDhyan do: 1 mL ghol ko 9 mL paani mein milane par **total 10 mL** hota hai, aur ghol **10 guna halka** hota hai. Agar 1 mL ghol mein 10 mL paani milaoge, to total 11 mL hoga aur ghol **11 guna** halka hoga, 10 guna nahi."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Quick Recap",
            "headingHinglish": "Quick Recap",
            "body": "- **Matter** = jiska **mass** hai aur jo **jagah** gherti hai. Hawa matter hai. Light, sound, heat aur feelings matter nahi hain.\n- Ulte glass wali activity se hawa **jagah gherti** hai, gubbare wali activity se hawa ka **mass** hota hai.\n- Matter **particles (kan)** se bana hai. Ye kan atoms ya molecules ho sakte hain (aage ke chapter \"Atoms and Molecules\" mein).\n- **Saboot 1:** Particles bahut chhote hain: ek crystal ya ink ki boond 5-8 baar 10 guna dilute karne par bhi rang deti hai. n steps mein ghol 10ⁿ guna halka hota hai.\n- **Saboot 2:** Particles ke beech jagah hai: cheeni ghulne par paani ka level lagbhag nahi badhta, syringe mein hawa dab jaati hai, do liquids mix hote hain.\n- **Saboot 3:** Particles hamesha harkat karte hain: diffusion (agarbatti, ink). Garmi badhane par harkat tez hoti hai, isliye diffusion tez hota hai (hamare example mein 3 guna).\n- **Saboot 4:** Particles ke beech aakarshan hota hai: lohe ki keel, chalk aur paani mein alag-alag taakat. Paani ki boondein judti hain.\n- Reshma ki agarbatti ki khushboo ka raaz: hawa ke kanon ke beech jagah + harkat + chhote kan = diffusion.",
            "bodyHinglish": "- **Matter** = jiska **mass** hai aur jo **jagah** gherti hai. Hawa matter hai. Light, sound, heat aur feelings matter nahi hain.\n- Ulte glass wali activity se hawa **jagah gherti** hai, gubbare wali activity se hawa ka **mass** hota hai.\n- Matter **particles (kan)** se bana hai. Ye kan atoms ya molecules ho sakte hain (aage ke chapter \"Atoms and Molecules\" mein).\n- **Saboot 1:** Particles bahut chhote hain: ek crystal ya ink ki boond 5-8 baar 10 guna dilute karne par bhi rang deti hai. n steps mein ghol 10ⁿ guna halka hota hai.\n- **Saboot 2:** Particles ke beech jagah hai: cheeni ghulne par paani ka level lagbhag nahi badhta, syringe mein hawa dab jaati hai, do liquids mix hote hain.\n- **Saboot 3:** Particles hamesha harkat karte hain: diffusion (agarbatti, ink). Garmi badhane par harkat tez hoti hai, isliye diffusion tez hota hai (hamare example mein 3 guna).\n- **Saboot 4:** Particles ke beech aakarshan hota hai: lohe ki keel, chalk aur paani mein alag-alag taakat. Paani ki boondein judti hain.\n- Reshma ki agarbatti ki khushboo ka raaz: hawa ke kanon ke beech jagah + harkat + chhote kan = diffusion."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Practice Questions",
            "headingHinglish": "Practice Questions",
            "body": "1. Define matter. Which of these are matter and which are not: sound, an iron nail, air, heat, a feeling of joy, milk?\n\n2. Describe a simple activity to show that air takes up space.\n\n3. A solution is diluted by taking 1 mL of it and mixing with 9 mL of water. This is repeated 4 times in total. By what factor is the original solution diluted? If its starting strength was 200 units, what is its strength at the end?\n\n4. 2 mL of a dye solution is mixed with 98 mL of water. By what factor has the solution been diluted?\n\n5. When sugar dissolves in water, the water level hardly rises. What does this tell us about the particles of water? Give one more activity that shows the same idea.\n\n6. In a syringe, air can be compressed easily but water cannot be compressed much. What does this suggest?\n\n7. A drop of ink takes 240 s to spread through a glass of cold water and 80 s through a glass of hot water. How many times faster is diffusion in hot water? What does this tell you about the particles?\n\n8. Explain why you can smell a freshly cooked sabzi from another room.\n\n9. Why does a steel wire not break easily, while a piece of chalk does? What property of particles is being shown?\n\n10. State True or False, and correct the false ones:\n    (a) Light is matter because it takes space.\n    (b) Diffusion happens only in gases.\n    (c) Particles of matter are constantly moving.\n    (d) Cold water shows faster diffusion than hot water.\n\n### Answers\n\n1. **Matter** wo hai jiska **mass** hota hai aur jo **jagah** gherta hai. **Matter hain:** iron nail, air, milk. **Matter nahi hain:** sound, heat, feeling of joy (ye sab energy ya feelings hain, inka mass aur volume nahi hota).\n\n2. Ek ulta glass lo, uske andar sookha tissue paper thoos do, aur glass ko seedha ulta karke paani se bhari bucket mein dabao. Tissue geela nahi hota, kyunki glass ke andar hawa jagah gherti hai aur paani ko andar nahi aane deti. Isse pata chalta hai ki **hawa jagah gherti hai**.\n\n3. Har step mein 10 guna dilution. 4 steps mein 10⁴ = **10000 guna**. Ant mein strength = 200 ÷ 10000 = **0.02 units**.\n   Jaanch: 200 ÷ 10 = 20; 20 ÷ 10 = 2; 2 ÷ 10 = 0.2; 0.2 ÷ 10 = 0.02 ✅\n\n4. Total volume = 2 mL + 98 mL = 100 mL. Dilution = 100 ÷ 2 = **50 guna**.\n   Jaanch: 2 mL ka 50 guna = 100 mL ✅\n\n5. Paani ke kanon ke beech **khaali jagah** hoti hai, jisme cheeni ke kan ghus jaate hain, isliye level lagbhag nahi badhta. Doosri activity: syringe mein hawa dabana, ya paani aur alcohol mix karke volume dekhna (volume thoda kam aata hai).\n\n6. Hawa ke kanon ke beech **bahut zyada jagah** hai, isliye dabane par kan paas aa jaate hain. Paani ke kanon ke beech **kam jagah** hai, isliye wo kam dabta hai.\n\n7. Garam paani mein diffusion = 240 ÷ 80 = **3 guna tez**.\n   Jaanch: 80 × 3 = 240 ✅. Matlab garam paani mein kan zyada tez harkat karte hain, isliye ink jaldi phailta hai.\n\n8. Sabzi ke kuch particles hawa mein mil jaate hain aur **diffusion** se harkat karte hue doosre kamre tak pahunch jaate hain. Jab wo naak tak aate hain, khushboo aati hai.\n\n9. Steel ke taar mein particles ke beech aakarshan (kheenchav) **bahut zyada** hai, isliye wo aasaani se nahi tootta. Chalk mein kheenchav kam hai, isliye wo toot jaata hai. Ye dikhata hai ki **particles ek doosre ko kheenchte hain, aur ye kheenchav alag cheezon mein alag hota hai.**\n\n10. (a) **False** ❌. Light energy hai, uska mass nahi hota aur wo jagah nahi gherti, isliye wo matter nahi hai. (b) **False** ❌. Diffusion liquids mein bhi hota hai (ink paani mein), bas dheere. (c) **True** ✅. (d) **False** ❌. Garam paani mein diffusion tez hota hai, thande mein dheema.\n\n---\n\nReshma ne ghar jaate hue socha ki aaj se wo har khushboo, har ghulti cheeni, har ink ki boond ko alag nazar se dekhegi: ye sab chhote-chhote kanon ke khel hain, jo harkat karte hain, ek doosre ke beech jagah banate hain aur ek doosre ko kheenchte hain.\n\n**Aage kya?** Reshma ne sir se poochha, \"Sir, lohe ki keel ke kan to ek doosre ko kas kar pakde hue the, par paani bahta hai, aur hawa to poore kamre mein phail gayi. Agar teeno cheezon ke kan wahi hain, to teeno itne alag kyun hain?\" Sir ne muskura kar kaha, \"Ye Topic 2 mein dekhenge: **Solid, Liquid aur Gas: Teen States ki Pehchaan.**\"",
            "bodyHinglish": "1. Define matter. Which of these are matter and which are not: sound, an iron nail, air, heat, a feeling of joy, milk?\n\n2. Describe a simple activity to show that air takes up space.\n\n3. A solution is diluted by taking 1 mL of it and mixing with 9 mL of water. This is repeated 4 times in total. By what factor is the original solution diluted? If its starting strength was 200 units, what is its strength at the end?\n\n4. 2 mL of a dye solution is mixed with 98 mL of water. By what factor has the solution been diluted?\n\n5. When sugar dissolves in water, the water level hardly rises. What does this tell us about the particles of water? Give one more activity that shows the same idea.\n\n6. In a syringe, air can be compressed easily but water cannot be compressed much. What does this suggest?\n\n7. A drop of ink takes 240 s to spread through a glass of cold water and 80 s through a glass of hot water. How many times faster is diffusion in hot water? What does this tell you about the particles?\n\n8. Explain why you can smell a freshly cooked sabzi from another room.\n\n9. Why does a steel wire not break easily, while a piece of chalk does? What property of particles is being shown?\n\n10. State True or False, and correct the false ones:\n    (a) Light is matter because it takes space.\n    (b) Diffusion happens only in gases.\n    (c) Particles of matter are constantly moving.\n    (d) Cold water shows faster diffusion than hot water.\n\n### Answers\n\n1. **Matter** wo hai jiska **mass** hota hai aur jo **jagah** gherta hai. **Matter hain:** iron nail, air, milk. **Matter nahi hain:** sound, heat, feeling of joy (ye sab energy ya feelings hain, inka mass aur volume nahi hota).\n\n2. Ek ulta glass lo, uske andar sookha tissue paper thoos do, aur glass ko seedha ulta karke paani se bhari bucket mein dabao. Tissue geela nahi hota, kyunki glass ke andar hawa jagah gherti hai aur paani ko andar nahi aane deti. Isse pata chalta hai ki **hawa jagah gherti hai**.\n\n3. Har step mein 10 guna dilution. 4 steps mein 10⁴ = **10000 guna**. Ant mein strength = 200 ÷ 10000 = **0.02 units**.\n   Jaanch: 200 ÷ 10 = 20; 20 ÷ 10 = 2; 2 ÷ 10 = 0.2; 0.2 ÷ 10 = 0.02 ✅\n\n4. Total volume = 2 mL + 98 mL = 100 mL. Dilution = 100 ÷ 2 = **50 guna**.\n   Jaanch: 2 mL ka 50 guna = 100 mL ✅\n\n5. Paani ke kanon ke beech **khaali jagah** hoti hai, jisme cheeni ke kan ghus jaate hain, isliye level lagbhag nahi badhta. Doosri activity: syringe mein hawa dabana, ya paani aur alcohol mix karke volume dekhna (volume thoda kam aata hai).\n\n6. Hawa ke kanon ke beech **bahut zyada jagah** hai, isliye dabane par kan paas aa jaate hain. Paani ke kanon ke beech **kam jagah** hai, isliye wo kam dabta hai.\n\n7. Garam paani mein diffusion = 240 ÷ 80 = **3 guna tez**.\n   Jaanch: 80 × 3 = 240 ✅. Matlab garam paani mein kan zyada tez harkat karte hain, isliye ink jaldi phailta hai.\n\n8. Sabzi ke kuch particles hawa mein mil jaate hain aur **diffusion** se harkat karte hue doosre kamre tak pahunch jaate hain. Jab wo naak tak aate hain, khushboo aati hai.\n\n9. Steel ke taar mein particles ke beech aakarshan (kheenchav) **bahut zyada** hai, isliye wo aasaani se nahi tootta. Chalk mein kheenchav kam hai, isliye wo toot jaata hai. Ye dikhata hai ki **particles ek doosre ko kheenchte hain, aur ye kheenchav alag cheezon mein alag hota hai.**\n\n10. (a) **False** ❌. Light energy hai, uska mass nahi hota aur wo jagah nahi gherti, isliye wo matter nahi hai. (b) **False** ❌. Diffusion liquids mein bhi hota hai (ink paani mein), bas dheere. (c) **True** ✅. (d) **False** ❌. Garam paani mein diffusion tez hota hai, thande mein dheema.\n\n---\n\nReshma ne ghar jaate hue socha ki aaj se wo har khushboo, har ghulti cheeni, har ink ki boond ko alag nazar se dekhegi: ye sab chhote-chhote kanon ke khel hain, jo harkat karte hain, ek doosre ke beech jagah banate hain aur ek doosre ko kheenchte hain.\n\n**Aage kya?** Reshma ne sir se poochha, \"Sir, lohe ki keel ke kan to ek doosre ko kas kar pakde hue the, par paani bahta hai, aur hawa to poore kamre mein phail gayi. Agar teeno cheezon ke kan wahi hain, to teeno itne alag kyun hain?\" Sir ne muskura kar kaha, \"Ye Topic 2 mein dekhenge: **Solid, Liquid aur Gas: Teen States ki Pehchaan.**\""
          }
