            "body": "Chapter 1 mein humne seekha ki har cheez **matter** hai, matter **particles (kan)** se bani hai, aur wahi particles kaise baithe hain us se solid, liquid ya gas ban jaata hai. Wahan hum zyadatar \"ek hi cheez\" ki baat kar rahe the: barf, paani, bhaap. Par ghar ke aas-paas dekho: doodh, hawa, samundar ka paani, mitti, sabzi ka salad. Kya ye sab bhi \"ek hi cheez\" hain? Ya inme kai cheezein mili hui hain? Is chapter ka sawaal yahi hai: **jo matter humein ghere hue hai, kya wo shuddh (pure) hai?** Aur sabse pehle ye samajhna hai ki science \"shuddh\" ka matlab kya leta hai.",
            "bodyHinglish": "Chapter 1 mein humne seekha ki har cheez **matter** hai, matter **particles (kan)** se bani hai, aur wahi particles kaise baithe hain us se solid, liquid ya gas ban jaata hai. Wahan hum zyadatar \"ek hi cheez\" ki baat kar rahe the: barf, paani, bhaap. Par ghar ke aas-paas dekho: doodh, hawa, samundar ka paani, mitti, sabzi ka salad. Kya ye sab bhi \"ek hi cheez\" hain? Ya inme kai cheezein mili hui hain? Is chapter ka sawaal yahi hai: **jo matter humein ghere hue hai, kya wo shuddh (pure) hai?** Aur sabse pehle ye samajhna hai ki science \"shuddh\" ka matlab kya leta hai."
