          {
            "heading": "Part A: Physical change: cheez wahi, roop alag",
            "headingHinglish": "Part A: Physical change: cheez wahi, roop alag",
            "body": "Physical change mein padaarth ka **naam, pehchan aur kaam wahi rehta hai**, bas uska bahari roop badalta hai: aakaar, size, state ya mixture ka hona. Particles ki jodi nahi badalti, sirf unka arrangement ya ek jagah se doosri jagah jaana badalta hai.\n\nKuch aam physical changes:\n\n- **State badalna:** barf ka paani, paani ki bhaap, kapoor ka seedha gas ban jaana (sublimation). Ye sab Chapter 1 mein dekhe the. Kulfi ka pighalna bhi yahi hai.\n- **Shape ya size badalna:** kaagaz ko phaadna, lakdi ko kaatna, chalk ko pees kar powder banana, dhaatu ko hathode se peet kar patra banana, taar kheench kar lamba karna.\n- **Dissolving:** namak ya cheeni ko paani mein ghol dena. Ye Topic 2 mein dekha tha. Ghol mein namak ya cheeni ke particles bas paani ke beech faile hain, naye padaarth nahi bane.\n- **Mixture banana aur alag karna:** Topic 4 aur 5 ke saare tareeke (chhaanna, filtration, distillation, crystallisation, magnet) **physical** tareeke hain, kyunki unse bas cheezein alag hoti hain, koi nayi cheez nahi banti.\n\n**Dissolving physical kyun hai?** Ek chhota numerical dekhte hain.\n\n**Example 1.** 20 g cheeni ko 100 g paani mein ghola. Ghol ka kul vazan kitna hoga? Phir sara paani evaporate kar do to kya bachega?\n\n- Ghol ka vazan = 20 g + 100 g = **120 g**.\n- Paani evaporate hone par (Chapter 1 wala evaporation) wapas bachegi **wahi 20 g cheeni** (crystals ke roop mein).\n\nCheeni wapas aa gayi, matlab cheeni kisi nayi cheez mein badli hi nahi thi: sirf paani mein chhup gayi thi. Isliye dissolving **physical change** hai. Jaanch: 20 + 100 = 120 ✅, aur sookhne par 20 g cheeni wahi wapas ✅\n\nPhysical change ki pehchan: aksar **reversible** hota hai (sab kuch palat sakta hai, jaise barf-paani-barf), aur naya padaarth nahi banta. Par ye \"aksar\" hai, \"hamesha\" nahi: kaagaz ke tukde karna palatna mushkil hai, phir bhi wo physical change hai, kyunki har tukda abhi bhi kaagaz hi hai.",
            "bodyHinglish": "Physical change mein padaarth ka **naam, pehchan aur kaam wahi rehta hai**, bas uska bahari roop badalta hai: aakaar, size, state ya mixture ka hona. Particles ki jodi nahi badalti, sirf unka arrangement ya ek jagah se doosri jagah jaana badalta hai.\n\nKuch aam physical changes:\n\n- **State badalna:** barf ka paani, paani ki bhaap, kapoor ka seedha gas ban jaana (sublimation). Ye sab Chapter 1 mein dekhe the. Kulfi ka pighalna bhi yahi hai.\n- **Shape ya size badalna:** kaagaz ko phaadna, lakdi ko kaatna, chalk ko pees kar powder banana, dhaatu ko hathode se peet kar patra banana, taar kheench kar lamba karna.\n- **Dissolving:** namak ya cheeni ko paani mein ghol dena. Ye Topic 2 mein dekha tha. Ghol mein namak ya cheeni ke particles bas paani ke beech faile hain, naye padaarth nahi bane.\n- **Mixture banana aur alag karna:** Topic 4 aur 5 ke saare tareeke (chhaanna, filtration, distillation, crystallisation, magnet) **physical** tareeke hain, kyunki unse bas cheezein alag hoti hain, koi nayi cheez nahi banti.\n\n**Dissolving physical kyun hai?** Ek chhota numerical dekhte hain.\n\n**Example 1.** 20 g cheeni ko 100 g paani mein ghola. Ghol ka kul vazan kitna hoga? Phir sara paani evaporate kar do to kya bachega?\n\n- Ghol ka vazan = 20 g + 100 g = **120 g**.\n- Paani evaporate hone par (Chapter 1 wala evaporation) wapas bachegi **wahi 20 g cheeni** (crystals ke roop mein).\n\nCheeni wapas aa gayi, matlab cheeni kisi nayi cheez mein badli hi nahi thi: sirf paani mein chhup gayi thi. Isliye dissolving **physical change** hai. Jaanch: 20 + 100 = 120 ✅, aur sookhne par 20 g cheeni wahi wapas ✅\n\nPhysical change ki pehchan: aksar **reversible** hota hai (sab kuch palat sakta hai, jaise barf-paani-barf), aur naya padaarth nahi banta. Par ye \"aksar\" hai, \"hamesha\" nahi: kaagaz ke tukde karna palatna mushkil hai, phir bhi wo physical change hai, kyunki har tukda abhi bhi kaagaz hi hai."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Part B: Chemical change: nayi cheez ka janm",
            "headingHinglish": "Part B: Chemical change: nayi cheez ka janm",
            "body": "Chemical change mein purani cheezein khatam hokar **nayi cheezein** banti hain, jinka **rang, gun, ya swaad** purani cheezon se alag hota hai.\n\nKuch chemical changes jo tum roz dekhte ho:\n\n- **Rusting (zang lagna):** loha + hawa + paani se bhoora, bhurbhura zang. Zang mein loha ke gun nahi hain: wo na chamakta hai, na kheencha jaata hai, na mudta hai, bas jhad jaata hai.\n- **Jalna (burning):** lakdi, kaagaz, LPG, mombatti jalte hain to raakh, dhuan aur gases ban jaate hain. Raakh ko wapas lakdi mein nahi badla ja sakta.\n- **Doodh ka phatna / dahi jamna:** doodh khatta hokar paneer jaisa ban jaata hai.\n- **Khaana pakana:** roti sekne par aate ka rang, swaad aur sakhti badal jaati hai; wo wapas aata nahi banti. Pakke chawal wapas kachche nahi ho sakte.\n- **Digestion (khaana hazam hona):** khaane ke bade kan pet mein chhote, naye padaarthon mein tootte hain jinhe sharir use kar sake.\n- **Fal ka pakna aur sadna:** kela peela aur narm hota hai, phir kaala; pakaa fal aur sadi hui sabzi ka swaad aur smell alag ho jaata hai.\n- **Iron + sulphur ko garam karna:** Topic 6 ki kaali, non-magnetic cheez, ek naya yaugik.\n\nChemical change ki pehchan: **naya padaarth** banta hai, aur aksar **irreversible** hota hai (palatna bahut mushkil ya bina khaas tareeke ke naamumkin).\n\n> **Chemical reaction ki ek jhalak:** jab bhi chemical change hota hai, use chemistry mein **chemical reaction** kehte hain. Purani cheezein (jaise loha, hawa, paani) **reactants** kehlaati hain aur nayi cheezein (zang) **products**. Reactions ko likhne ka tareeka, aur unke prakaar, tum Chapter 7 \"Chemical Changes and Reactions\" mein detail se seekhoge. Abhi bas ye pehchaanna kaafi hai ki kab nayi cheez bani.",
            "bodyHinglish": "Chemical change mein purani cheezein khatam hokar **nayi cheezein** banti hain, jinka **rang, gun, ya swaad** purani cheezon se alag hota hai.\n\nKuch chemical changes jo tum roz dekhte ho:\n\n- **Rusting (zang lagna):** loha + hawa + paani se bhoora, bhurbhura zang. Zang mein loha ke gun nahi hain: wo na chamakta hai, na kheencha jaata hai, na mudta hai, bas jhad jaata hai.\n- **Jalna (burning):** lakdi, kaagaz, LPG, mombatti jalte hain to raakh, dhuan aur gases ban jaate hain. Raakh ko wapas lakdi mein nahi badla ja sakta.\n- **Doodh ka phatna / dahi jamna:** doodh khatta hokar paneer jaisa ban jaata hai.\n- **Khaana pakana:** roti sekne par aate ka rang, swaad aur sakhti badal jaati hai; wo wapas aata nahi banti. Pakke chawal wapas kachche nahi ho sakte.\n- **Digestion (khaana hazam hona):** khaane ke bade kan pet mein chhote, naye padaarthon mein tootte hain jinhe sharir use kar sake.\n- **Fal ka pakna aur sadna:** kela peela aur narm hota hai, phir kaala; pakaa fal aur sadi hui sabzi ka swaad aur smell alag ho jaata hai.\n- **Iron + sulphur ko garam karna:** Topic 6 ki kaali, non-magnetic cheez, ek naya yaugik.\n\nChemical change ki pehchan: **naya padaarth** banta hai, aur aksar **irreversible** hota hai (palatna bahut mushkil ya bina khaas tareeke ke naamumkin).\n\n> **Chemical reaction ki ek jhalak:** jab bhi chemical change hota hai, use chemistry mein **chemical reaction** kehte hain. Purani cheezein (jaise loha, hawa, paani) **reactants** kehlaati hain aur nayi cheezein (zang) **products**. Reactions ko likhne ka tareeka, aur unke prakaar, tum Chapter 7 \"Chemical Changes and Reactions\" mein detail se seekhoge. Abhi bas ye pehchaanna kaafi hai ki kab nayi cheez bani."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Part C: Chemical change ke sanket (clues)",
            "headingHinglish": "Part C: Chemical change ke sanket (clues)",
            "body": "Naya padaarth banta hai ye aankh se seedha nahi dikhta, par kuch **sanket (clues)** hote hain jo humein shak karne ki wajah dete hain:\n\n```\n   CHEMICAL CHANGE ke clues\n\n        naya rang              gas / bubbles\n        (zang: bhoora)         (nimbu + baking soda)\n                 \\                 /\n                  \\               /\n                  +---------------+\n     nayi gandh --+ NAYA PADAARTH +-- garmi ya roshni\n  (doodh phatna)  +---------------+   (jalna)\n                          │\n                          v\n                thos nayi cheez banna\n               (doodh se paneer, zang)\n```\n\n> **Figure 7.1** – Chemical change ke paanch aam clues: naya rang, gas ya bubbles, nayi gandh, garmi ya roshni nikalna, aur koi nayi thos cheez banna.\n\nDhyan do: ye clues sirf **shak** dete hain, pakka saboot nahi. Kuch physical changes mein bhi inme se ek clue aa sakta hai:\n\n- **Paani ubalne par bubbles** aate hain, par wo bas paani ki bhaap hai: physical change.\n- **Bijli ke bulb ka filament** garam hokar chamakta hai aur garmi deta hai, par bulb band karne par wahi filament wapas aa jaata hai: physical change.\n- **Paani mein rang ghol dena:** rang naya dikhta hai, par wo bas dissolving hai.\n\nIsliye pakka sawaal ye hai: **\"Kya naya padaarth bana, jiska gun purane se alag ho?\"** Clues sirf shuruaati ishaara hain.",
            "bodyHinglish": "Naya padaarth banta hai ye aankh se seedha nahi dikhta, par kuch **sanket (clues)** hote hain jo humein shak karne ki wajah dete hain:\n\n```\n   CHEMICAL CHANGE ke clues\n\n        naya rang              gas / bubbles\n        (zang: bhoora)         (nimbu + baking soda)\n                 \\                 /\n                  \\               /\n                  +---------------+\n     nayi gandh --+ NAYA PADAARTH +-- garmi ya roshni\n  (doodh phatna)  +---------------+   (jalna)\n                          │\n                          v\n                thos nayi cheez banna\n               (doodh se paneer, zang)\n```\n\n> **Figure 7.1** – Chemical change ke paanch aam clues: naya rang, gas ya bubbles, nayi gandh, garmi ya roshni nikalna, aur koi nayi thos cheez banna.\n\nDhyan do: ye clues sirf **shak** dete hain, pakka saboot nahi. Kuch physical changes mein bhi inme se ek clue aa sakta hai:\n\n- **Paani ubalne par bubbles** aate hain, par wo bas paani ki bhaap hai: physical change.\n- **Bijli ke bulb ka filament** garam hokar chamakta hai aur garmi deta hai, par bulb band karne par wahi filament wapas aa jaata hai: physical change.\n- **Paani mein rang ghol dena:** rang naya dikhta hai, par wo bas dissolving hai.\n\nIsliye pakka sawaal ye hai: **\"Kya naya padaarth bana, jiska gun purane se alag ho?\"** Clues sirf shuruaati ishaara hain."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Part D: Tricky cases: dono badlaav ek saath",
            "headingHinglish": "Part D: Tricky cases: dono badlaav ek saath",
            "body": "**1. Jalti hui mombatti: dono!** Mombatti ka wax batti ke aas-paas pighalta hai (physical change, jam kar phir wax ban jaata hai). Par jo wax-bhaap batti ke dhaage ke paas lau mein jalti hai, wo naye padaarth (gases, thodi kaalikh) mein badal jaati hai: **chemical change**. Ek hi jagah par dono hota hai.\n\n**2. Anda ubalna:** Anda ubalne par andar ka paardarshi, behta hua hissa sakht aur safed ho jaata hai, aur peela hissa bhi jam jaata hai. Ab usse wapas kaccha anda nahi banaya ja sakta. Ye **chemical change** hai. (Ubalne ke liye paani ka garam hona physical hai, par anda khud badal gaya.)\n\n**3. Namak ko paani mein daalna:** Physical. Par agar kisi cheez ko paani mein daalne par bubbles, garmi ya naya rang aaye, to ye sirf dissolving nahi, ek reaction ho sakta hai. Isliye clues dekhna zaroori hai.\n\n**4. Sublimation (kapoor, naphthalene, dry ice):** Solid seedha gas ban gaya, par cheez wahi hai. **Physical.** Kapoor ko jalaya jaaye to wo chemical change hai, par wo alag baat hai.\n\n**5. Loha ko magnet banana:** Loha ke kan ek hi taraf sajte hain, par loha loha hi rehta hai: **physical.**\n\n**6. Mixture banana versus compound banana:** Topic 6 yaad karo. Iron + sulphur ko bas milana = physical (mixture). Garam karna = chemical (compound). Wahi do cheezein, par badlaav ka prakaar alag.",
            "bodyHinglish": "**1. Jalti hui mombatti: dono!** Mombatti ka wax batti ke aas-paas pighalta hai (physical change, jam kar phir wax ban jaata hai). Par jo wax-bhaap batti ke dhaage ke paas lau mein jalti hai, wo naye padaarth (gases, thodi kaalikh) mein badal jaati hai: **chemical change**. Ek hi jagah par dono hota hai.\n\n**2. Anda ubalna:** Anda ubalne par andar ka paardarshi, behta hua hissa sakht aur safed ho jaata hai, aur peela hissa bhi jam jaata hai. Ab usse wapas kaccha anda nahi banaya ja sakta. Ye **chemical change** hai. (Ubalne ke liye paani ka garam hona physical hai, par anda khud badal gaya.)\n\n**3. Namak ko paani mein daalna:** Physical. Par agar kisi cheez ko paani mein daalne par bubbles, garmi ya naya rang aaye, to ye sirf dissolving nahi, ek reaction ho sakta hai. Isliye clues dekhna zaroori hai.\n\n**4. Sublimation (kapoor, naphthalene, dry ice):** Solid seedha gas ban gaya, par cheez wahi hai. **Physical.** Kapoor ko jalaya jaaye to wo chemical change hai, par wo alag baat hai.\n\n**5. Loha ko magnet banana:** Loha ke kan ek hi taraf sajte hain, par loha loha hi rehta hai: **physical.**\n\n**6. Mixture banana versus compound banana:** Topic 6 yaad karo. Iron + sulphur ko bas milana = physical (mixture). Garam karna = chemical (compound). Wahi do cheezein, par badlaav ka prakaar alag."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Part E: Ghar par safe activities",
            "headingHinglish": "Part E: Ghar par safe activities",
            "body": "### Activity 1: Baking soda aur nimbu\n\n**Kya chahiye:** ek steel ya plastic ka glass, ek chammach baking soda, nimbu ka ras, thoda paani.\n\n**Kaise karein:**\n1. Glass mein ek chhoti chammach baking soda daalo.\n2. Dheere dheere nimbu ka ras daalo.\n3. Dekho: kya hua?\n\n**Kya dikhega:** turant **fizzing** hogi: bahut saare bubbles uthenge, aur kabhi glass thoda thanda mehsoos ho sakta hai. Ye bubbles ek **nayi gas** ke hain (carbon dioxide, naam yaad rakhna, formula aage seekhoge).\n\n**Kyun chemical change hai?** Baking soda aur nimbu ke khatte padaarth (acid) mil kar naye padaarth banate hain, jisme gas bhi hai. Gas ka banna naye padaarth ka sanket hai. Dobara se wahi baking soda aur nimbu ras wapas nahi mil sakte.\n\n**Safety:** Ye bilkul safe hai, par glass ko kisi **band bottle mein na karo** (gas bharne se dabav badh sakta hai). Khuli jagah, bade ki nigrani mein karo, aur aankhon mein ras na jaane do. Kuch chakhna nahi hai.\n\n**Control (tulna) ke liye:** Alag glass mein baking soda ko sirf paani mein dalo. Thoda sa ghulega, koi fizzing nahi hogi. Ye dissolving (physical) hai. Dono glass tulna karne par farak saaf dikhta hai.\n\n### Activity 2: Loha ki keel aur zang (kuch din ka prayog)\n\n**Kya chahiye:** teen saaf loha ki keelein (nail), teen shishe ke glass ya jar, paani, thoda sa tel ya cooking oil.\n\n**Kaise karein:**\n1. Glass A mein sookhi keel rakho (bina paani).\n2. Glass B mein keel ko aadhe se zyada paani mein dubo do.\n3. Glass C mein paani daalo, keel dubao, aur upar se paani ki satah par tel ki patli parat daal do (taaki paani mein hawa na ghule).\n4. Teeno glass ko 5 se 7 din tak chhod do, roz dekho.\n\n**Kya dikhega:** Glass B ki keel par, khaaskar paani ki satah ke paas, **bhoora zang** dikhega. A (sookhi) aur C (tel wali) mein zang bahut kam ya nahi hoga.\n\n**Kya seekha:** zang lagne ke liye **hawa (oxygen) aur paani** dono chahiye. Jahan inme se ek bhi nahi hai, wahan zang nahi laga. Isiliye gate par paint ya tel lagate hain: wo loha ko hawa aur paani se door rakhte hain. Samudra ke paas (namkeen hawa) zang aur tezi se lagta hai, isliye wahan gate jaldi kharab hote hain.\n\n**Safety:** zang lagi keelein haath mein sambhal ke pakdo, kati-chheel se bachao, aur kaam ke baad haath dho lo. **Kuch jalana nahi hai**; jalne wale kisi bhi prayog ko hamesha bade ke saath hi karo.",
            "bodyHinglish": "### Activity 1: Baking soda aur nimbu\n\n**Kya chahiye:** ek steel ya plastic ka glass, ek chammach baking soda, nimbu ka ras, thoda paani.\n\n**Kaise karein:**\n1. Glass mein ek chhoti chammach baking soda daalo.\n2. Dheere dheere nimbu ka ras daalo.\n3. Dekho: kya hua?\n\n**Kya dikhega:** turant **fizzing** hogi: bahut saare bubbles uthenge, aur kabhi glass thoda thanda mehsoos ho sakta hai. Ye bubbles ek **nayi gas** ke hain (carbon dioxide, naam yaad rakhna, formula aage seekhoge).\n\n**Kyun chemical change hai?** Baking soda aur nimbu ke khatte padaarth (acid) mil kar naye padaarth banate hain, jisme gas bhi hai. Gas ka banna naye padaarth ka sanket hai. Dobara se wahi baking soda aur nimbu ras wapas nahi mil sakte.\n\n**Safety:** Ye bilkul safe hai, par glass ko kisi **band bottle mein na karo** (gas bharne se dabav badh sakta hai). Khuli jagah, bade ki nigrani mein karo, aur aankhon mein ras na jaane do. Kuch chakhna nahi hai.\n\n**Control (tulna) ke liye:** Alag glass mein baking soda ko sirf paani mein dalo. Thoda sa ghulega, koi fizzing nahi hogi. Ye dissolving (physical) hai. Dono glass tulna karne par farak saaf dikhta hai.\n\n### Activity 2: Loha ki keel aur zang (kuch din ka prayog)\n\n**Kya chahiye:** teen saaf loha ki keelein (nail), teen shishe ke glass ya jar, paani, thoda sa tel ya cooking oil.\n\n**Kaise karein:**\n1. Glass A mein sookhi keel rakho (bina paani).\n2. Glass B mein keel ko aadhe se zyada paani mein dubo do.\n3. Glass C mein paani daalo, keel dubao, aur upar se paani ki satah par tel ki patli parat daal do (taaki paani mein hawa na ghule).\n4. Teeno glass ko 5 se 7 din tak chhod do, roz dekho.\n\n**Kya dikhega:** Glass B ki keel par, khaaskar paani ki satah ke paas, **bhoora zang** dikhega. A (sookhi) aur C (tel wali) mein zang bahut kam ya nahi hoga.\n\n**Kya seekha:** zang lagne ke liye **hawa (oxygen) aur paani** dono chahiye. Jahan inme se ek bhi nahi hai, wahan zang nahi laga. Isiliye gate par paint ya tel lagate hain: wo loha ko hawa aur paani se door rakhte hain. Samudra ke paas (namkeen hawa) zang aur tezi se lagta hai, isliye wahan gate jaldi kharab hote hain.\n\n**Safety:** zang lagi keelein haath mein sambhal ke pakdo, kati-chheel se bachao, aur kaam ke baad haath dho lo. **Kuch jalana nahi hai**; jalne wale kisi bhi prayog ko hamesha bade ke saath hi karo."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Part F: Physical aur chemical change ek tarazu mein",
            "headingHinglish": "Part F: Physical aur chemical change ek tarazu mein",
            "body": "| Pehlu | Physical change | Chemical change |\n|---|---|---|\n| Naya padaarth | Nahi banta | Banta hai |\n| Gun | Wahi rehte hain | Naye aur alag ho jaate hain |\n| Palatna | Aksar aasaan | Aksar mushkil ya naamumkin |\n| Particles ki pehchan | Wahi rehti hai | Nayi pehchan wale particles bante hain |\n| Garmi ya roshni | Kabhi kabhi (jaise filament), par zaroori nahi | Aksar nikalti ya jaati hai |\n| Example | Barf pighalna, cheeni ghulna, kaagaz phadna | Zang lagna, dahi jamna, khaana pakna, jalna |\n\n```\n        BADLAAV\n           │\n    Kya naya padaarth bana?\n      /              \\\n    NAHI             HAAN\n     │                 │\n PHYSICAL          CHEMICAL\n (kulfi pighli)    (gate par zang)\n```\n\n> **Figure 7.2** – Ek sawaal se faisla: \"kya naya padaarth bana?\" Nahi to physical change, haan to chemical change.",
            "bodyHinglish": "| Pehlu | Physical change | Chemical change |\n|---|---|---|\n| Naya padaarth | Nahi banta | Banta hai |\n| Gun | Wahi rehte hain | Naye aur alag ho jaate hain |\n| Palatna | Aksar aasaan | Aksar mushkil ya naamumkin |\n| Particles ki pehchan | Wahi rehti hai | Nayi pehchan wale particles bante hain |\n| Garmi ya roshni | Kabhi kabhi (jaise filament), par zaroori nahi | Aksar nikalti ya jaati hai |\n| Example | Barf pighalna, cheeni ghulna, kaagaz phadna | Zang lagna, dahi jamna, khaana pakna, jalna |\n\n```\n        BADLAAV\n           │\n    Kya naya padaarth bana?\n      /              \\\n    NAHI             HAAN\n     │                 │\n PHYSICAL          CHEMICAL\n (kulfi pighli)    (gate par zang)\n```\n\n> **Figure 7.2** – Ek sawaal se faisla: \"kya naya padaarth bana?\" Nahi to physical change, haan to chemical change."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Part G: Solved reasoning examples",
            "headingHinglish": "Part G: Solved reasoning examples",
            "body": "**Example 2. Neeche diye badlaav physical hain ya chemical?** (a) Chalk ko pees kar powder banana, (b) paneer ke liye doodh phatna, (c) sooraj ki garmi se samudra ka paani sookhna, (d) loha ke gate par zang lagna, (e) cheeni ko tawe par garam karte hue kaala hona.\n\n- (a) **Physical.** Chalk ke tukde chote hue par chalk wahi hai.\n- (b) **Chemical.** Doodh khatta ho kar paneer aur paani mein badla; naya padaarth bana, wapas doodh nahi banta.\n- (c) **Physical.** Paani bhaap ban gaya (evaporation), namak peeche bacha; ye wapas paani mein badla ja sakta hai.\n- (d) **Chemical.** Zang ek nayi cheez hai, loha nahi.\n- (e) **Chemical.** Cheeni jal kar kaali ho gayi: naya padaarth bana, wapas cheeni nahi mil sakti. (Garam karne par cheeni pehle pighalti bhi hai, wo hissa physical hai.)\n\n**Example 3. Raunak kehta hai: \"Bubbles uthe, isliye ye pakka chemical change hai.\" Kya Raunak theek hai?**\n\nNahi. Ubalte paani mein bhi bubbles uthte hain, par wo bas paani ki bhaap hai, naya padaarth nahi. Pakka sawal ye hai ki **naya padaarth bana ya nahi.** Nimbu aur baking soda mein bubbles naye gas ke the, isliye wahan chemical change tha; ubalte paani mein wahi paani gas ban gaya, isliye wahan physical.\n\n**Example 4. Ek mombatti ka wax pighal kar neeche jam gaya. Phir batti ke upar ka wax jal gaya. Kaun sa physical, kaun sa chemical?**\n\nPighal kar jamna: **physical**, kyunki wax wahi hai, ye palat sakta hai (dobara pighla sakte ho). Lau mein jalna: **chemical**, kyunki wax ki bhaap naye padaarthon mein badal gayi (gases aur kaalikh) jo wapas wax nahi bante.",
            "bodyHinglish": "**Example 2. Neeche diye badlaav physical hain ya chemical?** (a) Chalk ko pees kar powder banana, (b) paneer ke liye doodh phatna, (c) sooraj ki garmi se samudra ka paani sookhna, (d) loha ke gate par zang lagna, (e) cheeni ko tawe par garam karte hue kaala hona.\n\n- (a) **Physical.** Chalk ke tukde chote hue par chalk wahi hai.\n- (b) **Chemical.** Doodh khatta ho kar paneer aur paani mein badla; naya padaarth bana, wapas doodh nahi banta.\n- (c) **Physical.** Paani bhaap ban gaya (evaporation), namak peeche bacha; ye wapas paani mein badla ja sakta hai.\n- (d) **Chemical.** Zang ek nayi cheez hai, loha nahi.\n- (e) **Chemical.** Cheeni jal kar kaali ho gayi: naya padaarth bana, wapas cheeni nahi mil sakti. (Garam karne par cheeni pehle pighalti bhi hai, wo hissa physical hai.)\n\n**Example 3. Raunak kehta hai: \"Bubbles uthe, isliye ye pakka chemical change hai.\" Kya Raunak theek hai?**\n\nNahi. Ubalte paani mein bhi bubbles uthte hain, par wo bas paani ki bhaap hai, naya padaarth nahi. Pakka sawal ye hai ki **naya padaarth bana ya nahi.** Nimbu aur baking soda mein bubbles naye gas ke the, isliye wahan chemical change tha; ubalte paani mein wahi paani gas ban gaya, isliye wahan physical.\n\n**Example 4. Ek mombatti ka wax pighal kar neeche jam gaya. Phir batti ke upar ka wax jal gaya. Kaun sa physical, kaun sa chemical?**\n\nPighal kar jamna: **physical**, kyunki wax wahi hai, ye palat sakta hai (dobara pighla sakte ho). Lau mein jalna: **chemical**, kyunki wax ki bhaap naye padaarthon mein badal gayi (gases aur kaalikh) jo wapas wax nahi bante."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Part H: Chapter Ka Saar: poore chapter ka hisaab",
            "headingHinglish": "Part H: Chapter Ka Saar: poore chapter ka hisaab",
            "body": "Chapter ke shuru mein humne \"shuddh\" ka matlab dekha tha. Phir ek tree banta gaya:\n\n```\n                     MATTER\n                       │\n          +------------+------------+\n          │                         │\n   PURE SUBSTANCE               MIXTURE\n          │                         │\n    +-----+-----+           +-------+-------+\n    │           │           │               │\n ELEMENT    COMPOUND   HOMOGENEOUS     HETEROGENEOUS\n (loha,     (paani,    (solution,      (suspension,\n  sona)      namak)     alloy)          colloid)\n```\n\n> **Figure 7.3** – Poore chapter ka tree: matter ya to pure substance (element ya compound) hai, ya mixture (homogeneous ya heterogeneous). Colloid dikhne mein ek jaisa lagta hai, par Topic 3 ke hisaab se wo heterogeneous mein aata hai.\n\nEk nazar mein Chapter 2 ka saara hisaab:\n\n| Topic | Kya seekha | Ek line |\n|---|---|---|\n| Topic 1 | Pure aur mixture | Science mein \"pure\" ka matlab ek hi tarah ka padaarth; mixture mein kai padaarth mile hote hain jo apne gun rakhte hain, aur wo homogeneous ya heterogeneous ho sakte hain. |\n| Topic 2 | Solutions | Solution ek homogeneous mixture hai (solute + solvent); concentration percent mein napi jaati hai; saturated solution aur solubility temperature par nirbhar karti hai. |\n| Topic 3 | Suspension aur colloid | Suspension mein kan dikhte aur beth jaate hain; colloid mein kan chhote par roshni ko bikherte hain (Tyndall effect); solution mein sabse chhote. |\n| Topic 4 | Mixtures alag karna 1 | Jis gun mein farak ho, wahi tareeka chuno: haath se chunna, soop se phatakna, chhalni, magnet, neeche baithne dena aur upar ka paani ulatna (decantation), filtration, centrifuge, separating funnel, evaporation, sublimation. |\n| Topic 5 | Mixtures alag karna 2 | Crystallisation, distillation, fractional distillation aur chromatography se mushkil mixtures alag hote hain. |\n| Topic 6 | Tatva aur yaugik | Tatva ek hi tarah ke kan ka hota hai aur toda nahi jaa sakta; yaugik mein tatva fixed ratio mein jud kar naye gun banate hain; mixture aur compound mein farak. |\n| Topic 7 | Physical aur chemical change | Physical mein naya padaarth nahi banta, chemical mein banta hai; gas, rang, gandh, garmi aur thos naya padaarth ke clues hain. |\n\nEshan ne kulfi ka akhri tukda khaya aur gate ko dekha, jo ab chamakta hua paint hone ki taiyaari mein tha. \"Uncle, ab samajh aaya: kulfi ka pighalna bas roop ka badlaav tha, par zang ek nayi cheez thi.\" Mr. Shetty muskuraye, \"Ab tu sahi sochne laga.\"",
            "bodyHinglish": "Chapter ke shuru mein humne \"shuddh\" ka matlab dekha tha. Phir ek tree banta gaya:\n\n```\n                     MATTER\n                       │\n          +------------+------------+\n          │                         │\n   PURE SUBSTANCE               MIXTURE\n          │                         │\n    +-----+-----+           +-------+-------+\n    │           │           │               │\n ELEMENT    COMPOUND   HOMOGENEOUS     HETEROGENEOUS\n (loha,     (paani,    (solution,      (suspension,\n  sona)      namak)     alloy)          colloid)\n```\n\n> **Figure 7.3** – Poore chapter ka tree: matter ya to pure substance (element ya compound) hai, ya mixture (homogeneous ya heterogeneous). Colloid dikhne mein ek jaisa lagta hai, par Topic 3 ke hisaab se wo heterogeneous mein aata hai.\n\nEk nazar mein Chapter 2 ka saara hisaab:\n\n| Topic | Kya seekha | Ek line |\n|---|---|---|\n| Topic 1 | Pure aur mixture | Science mein \"pure\" ka matlab ek hi tarah ka padaarth; mixture mein kai padaarth mile hote hain jo apne gun rakhte hain, aur wo homogeneous ya heterogeneous ho sakte hain. |\n| Topic 2 | Solutions | Solution ek homogeneous mixture hai (solute + solvent); concentration percent mein napi jaati hai; saturated solution aur solubility temperature par nirbhar karti hai. |\n| Topic 3 | Suspension aur colloid | Suspension mein kan dikhte aur beth jaate hain; colloid mein kan chhote par roshni ko bikherte hain (Tyndall effect); solution mein sabse chhote. |\n| Topic 4 | Mixtures alag karna 1 | Jis gun mein farak ho, wahi tareeka chuno: haath se chunna, soop se phatakna, chhalni, magnet, neeche baithne dena aur upar ka paani ulatna (decantation), filtration, centrifuge, separating funnel, evaporation, sublimation. |\n| Topic 5 | Mixtures alag karna 2 | Crystallisation, distillation, fractional distillation aur chromatography se mushkil mixtures alag hote hain. |\n| Topic 6 | Tatva aur yaugik | Tatva ek hi tarah ke kan ka hota hai aur toda nahi jaa sakta; yaugik mein tatva fixed ratio mein jud kar naye gun banate hain; mixture aur compound mein farak. |\n| Topic 7 | Physical aur chemical change | Physical mein naya padaarth nahi banta, chemical mein banta hai; gas, rang, gandh, garmi aur thos naya padaarth ke clues hain. |\n\nEshan ne kulfi ka akhri tukda khaya aur gate ko dekha, jo ab chamakta hua paint hone ki taiyaari mein tha. \"Uncle, ab samajh aaya: kulfi ka pighalna bas roop ka badlaav tha, par zang ek nayi cheez thi.\" Mr. Shetty muskuraye, \"Ab tu sahi sochne laga.\""
          },
          {
            "heading": "Aam galtiyan (bachke rehna)",
            "headingHinglish": "Aam galtiyan (bachke rehna)",
            "body": "**Galti 1: \"Jo badlaav palat jaaye wahi physical hai aur jo na palte wahi chemical\"**\n\nYe lagbhag sahi hai, par pakka rule nahi. Kaagaz ko phaadna palatna mushkil hai, par wo physical hai. Isliye asli sawal hai: **\"Naya padaarth bana?\"**\n\n**Galti 2: \"Gas ke bubbles dikhe, matlab chemical change\"**\n\nUbalte paani ke bubbles bhaap ke hain, naya padaarth nahi. Clues sirf shak dete hain.\n\n**Galti 3: \"Dissolving ek chemical change hai kyunki cheeni gayab ho gayi\"**\n\nCheeni gayab nahi hui, paani mein faili hui hai. Paani sookhne par cheeni wapas milti hai. Ye physical change hai.\n\n**Galti 4: \"Garmi ya roshni nikle to chemical change hi hoga\"**\n\nBijli ke bulb ka filament garam hokar chamakta hai, par wahi filament bana rehta hai. Physical.\n\n**Galti 5: \"Mombatti sirf chemical change hai\"**\n\nWax ka pighalna physical hai aur uska jalna chemical hai. Ek hi cheez mein dono ho sakte hain.\n\n**Galti 6: \"Chemical change ka matlab hamesha khatarnak ya zehrili cheez\"**\n\nNahi. Roti sekna, khaana hazam hona aur dahi jamna, sab chemical change hain aur roz ki zindagi ka hissa hain.",
            "bodyHinglish": "**Galti 1: \"Jo badlaav palat jaaye wahi physical hai aur jo na palte wahi chemical\"**\n\nYe lagbhag sahi hai, par pakka rule nahi. Kaagaz ko phaadna palatna mushkil hai, par wo physical hai. Isliye asli sawal hai: **\"Naya padaarth bana?\"**\n\n**Galti 2: \"Gas ke bubbles dikhe, matlab chemical change\"**\n\nUbalte paani ke bubbles bhaap ke hain, naya padaarth nahi. Clues sirf shak dete hain.\n\n**Galti 3: \"Dissolving ek chemical change hai kyunki cheeni gayab ho gayi\"**\n\nCheeni gayab nahi hui, paani mein faili hui hai. Paani sookhne par cheeni wapas milti hai. Ye physical change hai.\n\n**Galti 4: \"Garmi ya roshni nikle to chemical change hi hoga\"**\n\nBijli ke bulb ka filament garam hokar chamakta hai, par wahi filament bana rehta hai. Physical.\n\n**Galti 5: \"Mombatti sirf chemical change hai\"**\n\nWax ka pighalna physical hai aur uska jalna chemical hai. Ek hi cheez mein dono ho sakte hain.\n\n**Galti 6: \"Chemical change ka matlab hamesha khatarnak ya zehrili cheez\"**\n\nNahi. Roti sekna, khaana hazam hona aur dahi jamna, sab chemical change hain aur roz ki zindagi ka hissa hain."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Quick Recap",
            "headingHinglish": "Quick Recap",
            "body": "- **Physical change:** naya padaarth nahi banta; cheez wahi rehti hai, bas aakaar, size, state ya mixture badalta hai. Aksar reversible. Misaal: pighalna, dissolving, kaagaz phadna, sublimation.\n- **Chemical change:** naya padaarth banta hai jiske gun alag hote hain. Aksar irreversible. Misaal: zang, jalna, doodh phatna, khaana pakna, digestion. Ise chemical reaction bhi kehte hain (Chapter 7 mein poori tarah).\n- **Clues:** naya rang, gas ya bubbles, nayi gandh, garmi ya roshni, nayi thos cheez. Ye sirf shak dete hain: ubalte paani ke bubbles aur bulb ke filament ki roshni physical change hain.\n- **Tricky cases:** mombatti mein dono badlaav; anda ubalna chemical; dissolving aur sublimation physical.\n- **Zang** ke liye hawa aur paani dono chahiye; paint ya tel unhe loha se door rakhte hain.\n- **Chapter ka saar:** matter ya to pure substance (element, compound) hai ya mixture (homogeneous, heterogeneous). Mixtures ko unke alag gun ke aadhaar par physical tareeke se alag karte hain; compound ko alag karne ke liye chemical change chahiye.",
            "bodyHinglish": "- **Physical change:** naya padaarth nahi banta; cheez wahi rehti hai, bas aakaar, size, state ya mixture badalta hai. Aksar reversible. Misaal: pighalna, dissolving, kaagaz phadna, sublimation.\n- **Chemical change:** naya padaarth banta hai jiske gun alag hote hain. Aksar irreversible. Misaal: zang, jalna, doodh phatna, khaana pakna, digestion. Ise chemical reaction bhi kehte hain (Chapter 7 mein poori tarah).\n- **Clues:** naya rang, gas ya bubbles, nayi gandh, garmi ya roshni, nayi thos cheez. Ye sirf shak dete hain: ubalte paani ke bubbles aur bulb ke filament ki roshni physical change hain.\n- **Tricky cases:** mombatti mein dono badlaav; anda ubalna chemical; dissolving aur sublimation physical.\n- **Zang** ke liye hawa aur paani dono chahiye; paint ya tel unhe loha se door rakhte hain.\n- **Chapter ka saar:** matter ya to pure substance (element, compound) hai ya mixture (homogeneous, heterogeneous). Mixtures ko unke alag gun ke aadhaar par physical tareeke se alag karte hain; compound ko alag karne ke liye chemical change chahiye."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Practice Questions",
            "headingHinglish": "Practice Questions",
            "body": "1. Define physical change and chemical change. Give two examples of each.\n\n2. Classify as physical or chemical: (a) melting of ice cream, (b) milk turning sour, (c) tearing a sheet of paper, (d) cooking rice, (e) dissolving salt in water, (f) camphor disappearing from an open dish.\n\n3. List any four clues that a chemical change may have taken place. Why are they called \"clues\" and not proof?\n\n4. A student drops baking soda into lemon juice and sees bubbles. Another student boils water and also sees bubbles. Why is one a chemical change and the other not?\n\n5. 30 g of salt is dissolved in 120 g of water. (a) What is the mass of the solution? (b) If all the water is evaporated, how much salt will be left? (c) Is dissolving a physical or a chemical change? Explain using your answers.\n\n6. A burning candle shows both a physical and a chemical change. Identify each.\n\n7. Explain with one reason why iron nails kept in dry air rust much less than nails kept in damp air. Suggest two ways to protect an iron gate from rusting.\n\n8. Is separating a mixture of iron filings and sulphur with a magnet a physical or a chemical change? What about heating the same mixture strongly?\n\n9. State True or False, and correct the false ones:\n   (a) In a physical change a new substance is always formed.\n   (b) Rusting is a chemical change.\n   (c) Every change that is hard to reverse is a chemical change.\n   (d) A glowing bulb filament shows a chemical change because it gives off light.\n\n10. Make a tree diagram showing how all matter is classified in this chapter, from matter down to element, compound, homogeneous mixture and heterogeneous mixture. Give one example at each end.\n\n### Answers\n\n1. **Physical change:** wo badlaav jisme koi naya padaarth nahi banta (barf pighalna, kaagaz phadna). **Chemical change:** wo badlaav jisme naya padaarth banta hai jiske gun alag hote hain (zang lagna, doodh phatna).\n\n2. (a) **Physical**: ice cream wahi hai, bas thos se tarl. (b) **Chemical**: nayi gandh, naya swaad, naye padaarth. (c) **Physical**: kaagaz abhi bhi kaagaz hai. (d) **Chemical**: chawal ka swaad aur gun badal jaate hain. (e) **Physical**: namak paani sookhne par wapas milta hai. (f) **Physical** (sublimation): solid seedha gas bana, wahi camphor.\n\n3. Clues: naya rang, gas ya bubbles, nayi gandh, garmi ya roshni, nayi thos cheez banna (koi bhi chaar). Inhe \"clues\" isliye kehte hain kyunki physical change mein bhi inme se kuch aa sakte hain (ubalte paani ke bubbles, bulb ki roshni). Pakka saboot hai **naya padaarth banna**.\n\n4. Baking soda aur nimbu ke ras mein bubbles ek **naye gas** ke hain, isliye chemical change. Ubalte paani mein bubbles wahi paani ki bhaap hain: sirf state badli, naya padaarth nahi, isliye physical.\n\n5. (a) 30 + 120 = **150 g**. (b) Evaporate hone par wahi **30 g namak** bachega. (c) **Physical change**: namak badla nahi, wapas mil gaya. Jaanch: 30 + 120 = 150 ✅ aur 30 g wapas = shuruat jaisa ✅\n\n6. Wax ka pighalna aur dobara jamna = **physical**. Batti ke paas wax ki bhaap ka lau mein jalna (gases aur kaalikh ban-na) = **chemical**.\n\n7. Zang ke liye **hawa aur paani (nami)** dono chahiye. Sookhi hawa mein nami kam hoti hai, isliye zang kam lagta hai. Bachaane ke tareeke: **paint karna**, **tel ya grease lagana** (kisi bhi do).\n\n8. Magnet se alag karna **physical** hai (dono cheezein wahi hain, bas alag hui). Strong garam karna **chemical** hai (nayi kaali cheez banti hai).\n\n9. (a) **False** ❌. Physical change mein naya padaarth nahi banta; chemical change mein banta hai. (b) **True** ✅. Zang naya padaarth hai. (c) **False** ❌. Kaagaz phadna palatna mushkil hai par physical hai. (d) **False** ❌. Filament garam hokar roshni deta hai par wahi filament rehta hai: physical.\n\n10. Matter se do shaakhaein: **Pure substance** aur **Mixture**. Pure substance se **Element** (jaise loha, sona) aur **Compound** (jaise paani, namak). Mixture se **Homogeneous** (jaise namak ka ghol, brass) aur **Heterogeneous** (jaise mitti-paani, salad).\n\n---\n\nShabaash! Ab tumhe pata hai ki kisi bhi badlaav ko dekh kar kaise poochna hai: \"kya kuch naya bana?\" Aur ek poore chapter mein tumne \"shuddh\" ka asli matlab, mixtures ko alag karne ke tareeke aur tatva-yaugik ka farak samjha.\n\n**Aage kya?** Ab tak humne \"loha\", \"sulphur\", \"oxygen\" jaise tatvon ke naam shabdon mein liye. Agle chapter **\"Language of Chemistry\"** mein hum seekhenge ki ek tatva ka naam chemistry mein chhote symbol ke saath kaise likhte hain, aur yaugik ke formulae kaise bante hain.",
            "bodyHinglish": "1. Define physical change and chemical change. Give two examples of each.\n\n2. Classify as physical or chemical: (a) melting of ice cream, (b) milk turning sour, (c) tearing a sheet of paper, (d) cooking rice, (e) dissolving salt in water, (f) camphor disappearing from an open dish.\n\n3. List any four clues that a chemical change may have taken place. Why are they called \"clues\" and not proof?\n\n4. A student drops baking soda into lemon juice and sees bubbles. Another student boils water and also sees bubbles. Why is one a chemical change and the other not?\n\n5. 30 g of salt is dissolved in 120 g of water. (a) What is the mass of the solution? (b) If all the water is evaporated, how much salt will be left? (c) Is dissolving a physical or a chemical change? Explain using your answers.\n\n6. A burning candle shows both a physical and a chemical change. Identify each.\n\n7. Explain with one reason why iron nails kept in dry air rust much less than nails kept in damp air. Suggest two ways to protect an iron gate from rusting.\n\n8. Is separating a mixture of iron filings and sulphur with a magnet a physical or a chemical change? What about heating the same mixture strongly?\n\n9. State True or False, and correct the false ones:\n   (a) In a physical change a new substance is always formed.\n   (b) Rusting is a chemical change.\n   (c) Every change that is hard to reverse is a chemical change.\n   (d) A glowing bulb filament shows a chemical change because it gives off light.\n\n10. Make a tree diagram showing how all matter is classified in this chapter, from matter down to element, compound, homogeneous mixture and heterogeneous mixture. Give one example at each end.\n\n### Answers\n\n1. **Physical change:** wo badlaav jisme koi naya padaarth nahi banta (barf pighalna, kaagaz phadna). **Chemical change:** wo badlaav jisme naya padaarth banta hai jiske gun alag hote hain (zang lagna, doodh phatna).\n\n2. (a) **Physical**: ice cream wahi hai, bas thos se tarl. (b) **Chemical**: nayi gandh, naya swaad, naye padaarth. (c) **Physical**: kaagaz abhi bhi kaagaz hai. (d) **Chemical**: chawal ka swaad aur gun badal jaate hain. (e) **Physical**: namak paani sookhne par wapas milta hai. (f) **Physical** (sublimation): solid seedha gas bana, wahi camphor.\n\n3. Clues: naya rang, gas ya bubbles, nayi gandh, garmi ya roshni, nayi thos cheez banna (koi bhi chaar). Inhe \"clues\" isliye kehte hain kyunki physical change mein bhi inme se kuch aa sakte hain (ubalte paani ke bubbles, bulb ki roshni). Pakka saboot hai **naya padaarth banna**.\n\n4. Baking soda aur nimbu ke ras mein bubbles ek **naye gas** ke hain, isliye chemical change. Ubalte paani mein bubbles wahi paani ki bhaap hain: sirf state badli, naya padaarth nahi, isliye physical.\n\n5. (a) 30 + 120 = **150 g**. (b) Evaporate hone par wahi **30 g namak** bachega. (c) **Physical change**: namak badla nahi, wapas mil gaya. Jaanch: 30 + 120 = 150 ✅ aur 30 g wapas = shuruat jaisa ✅\n\n6. Wax ka pighalna aur dobara jamna = **physical**. Batti ke paas wax ki bhaap ka lau mein jalna (gases aur kaalikh ban-na) = **chemical**.\n\n7. Zang ke liye **hawa aur paani (nami)** dono chahiye. Sookhi hawa mein nami kam hoti hai, isliye zang kam lagta hai. Bachaane ke tareeke: **paint karna**, **tel ya grease lagana** (kisi bhi do).\n\n8. Magnet se alag karna **physical** hai (dono cheezein wahi hain, bas alag hui). Strong garam karna **chemical** hai (nayi kaali cheez banti hai).\n\n9. (a) **False** ❌. Physical change mein naya padaarth nahi banta; chemical change mein banta hai. (b) **True** ✅. Zang naya padaarth hai. (c) **False** ❌. Kaagaz phadna palatna mushkil hai par physical hai. (d) **False** ❌. Filament garam hokar roshni deta hai par wahi filament rehta hai: physical.\n\n10. Matter se do shaakhaein: **Pure substance** aur **Mixture**. Pure substance se **Element** (jaise loha, sona) aur **Compound** (jaise paani, namak). Mixture se **Homogeneous** (jaise namak ka ghol, brass) aur **Heterogeneous** (jaise mitti-paani, salad).\n\n---\n\nShabaash! Ab tumhe pata hai ki kisi bhi badlaav ko dekh kar kaise poochna hai: \"kya kuch naya bana?\" Aur ek poore chapter mein tumne \"shuddh\" ka asli matlab, mixtures ko alag karne ke tareeke aur tatva-yaugik ka farak samjha.\n\n**Aage kya?** Ab tak humne \"loha\", \"sulphur\", \"oxygen\" jaise tatvon ke naam shabdon mein liye. Agle chapter **\"Language of Chemistry\"** mein hum seekhenge ki ek tatva ka naam chemistry mein chhote symbol ke saath kaise likhte hain, aur yaugik ke formulae kaise bante hain."
          }
