            "heading": "Part A: Symbols ki zaroorat kyun padi?",
            "headingHinglish": "Part A: Symbols ki zaroorat kyun padi?",
            "body": "Abhi tak jaane gaye tatvon ki ginti sau se bhi upar hai (lagbhag 118, ye humne pichhle chapter mein dekha tha). Agar har baar naam poora likhna pade to teen dikkatein aati hain:\n\n1. **Samay aur jagah:** \"Magnesium\" likhna \"Mg\" se kaafi lamba hai. Ek lambi reaction mein ye naam sau baar aa sakte hain.\n2. **Bhasha ka fark:** Sodium ko Hindi mein, Tamil mein, Japanese mein alag naam se bula sakte hain. Par agar sab \"Na\" likhein, to koi bhi padh sakta hai.\n3. **Aage ka kaam:** Aage is chapter mein hum \"formula\" aur \"equation\" likhenge, jahan ek line mein kai tatva aayenge. Wahan chhote symbols ke bina kaam chalega hi nahi.\n\nIsliye vaigyanikon ne ek **common, chhoti bhasha** banayi. Jaise ganit mein +, −, = poori duniya ke liye ek hi hain, waise hi tatvon ke symbols bhi.",
            "bodyHinglish": "Abhi tak jaane gaye tatvon ki ginti sau se bhi upar hai (lagbhag 118, ye humne pichhle chapter mein dekha tha). Agar har baar naam poora likhna pade to teen dikkatein aati hain:\n\n1. **Samay aur jagah:** \"Magnesium\" likhna \"Mg\" se kaafi lamba hai. Ek lambi reaction mein ye naam sau baar aa sakte hain.\n2. **Bhasha ka fark:** Sodium ko Hindi mein, Tamil mein, Japanese mein alag naam se bula sakte hain. Par agar sab \"Na\" likhein, to koi bhi padh sakta hai.\n3. **Aage ka kaam:** Aage is chapter mein hum \"formula\" aur \"equation\" likhenge, jahan ek line mein kai tatva aayenge. Wahan chhote symbols ke bina kaam chalega hi nahi.\n\nIsliye vaigyanikon ne ek **common, chhoti bhasha** banayi. Jaise ganit mein +, −, = poori duniya ke liye ek hi hain, waise hi tatvon ke symbols bhi."
