            "heading": "Part B: Symbols ki chhoti si kahani",
            "headingHinglish": "Part B: Symbols ki chhoti si kahani",
            "body": "**Dalton ki tasveerein.** Lagbhag 200 saal pehle John Dalton (wahi jinhone aage ke chapter mein aane wali atomic theory di) ne har tatva ke liye ek chhoti **tasveer** (gol, kuch andar ke nishaan wale chhote circle) banayi thi. Hydrogen ke liye ek dot wala circle, sulphur ke liye ek aur nishaan, aur isi tarah baaki. Dikkat ye thi ki ye tasveerein yaad rakhna, copy karna aur chhapna mushkil tha, aur do log ek hi tasveer ko alag banate the.\n\n**Berzelius ke akshar.** Phir Swedish vaigyanik **Jöns Jacob Berzelius** ne ek bahut aasaan idea diya: **tatva ke naam ke pehle akshar (ya pehle do akshar) ko hi uska symbol bana do.** Akshar sabko aate hain, alag-alag keyboard par type ho jaate hain, aur copy karna bhi aasaan. Aaj poori duniya yahi tarika use karti hai. Naye tatvon ke symbol aaj bhi ek antarrashtriya sanstha (international group of chemists) tay karti hai, taaki poori duniya mein ek hi symbol rahe.",
            "bodyHinglish": "**Dalton ki tasveerein.** Lagbhag 200 saal pehle John Dalton (wahi jinhone aage ke chapter mein aane wali atomic theory di) ne har tatva ke liye ek chhoti **tasveer** (gol, kuch andar ke nishaan wale chhote circle) banayi thi. Hydrogen ke liye ek dot wala circle, sulphur ke liye ek aur nishaan, aur isi tarah baaki. Dikkat ye thi ki ye tasveerein yaad rakhna, copy karna aur chhapna mushkil tha, aur do log ek hi tasveer ko alag banate the.\n\n**Berzelius ke akshar.** Phir Swedish vaigyanik **Jöns Jacob Berzelius** ne ek bahut aasaan idea diya: **tatva ke naam ke pehle akshar (ya pehle do akshar) ko hi uska symbol bana do.** Akshar sabko aate hain, alag-alag keyboard par type ho jaate hain, aur copy karna bhi aasaan. Aaj poori duniya yahi tarika use karti hai. Naye tatvon ke symbol aaj bhi ek antarrashtriya sanstha (international group of chemists) tay karti hai, taaki poori duniya mein ek hi symbol rahe."
