            "bodyHinglish": "Pichhle topic mein humne radicals ki do tables yaad ki: positive charge wale (Na⁺, Ca²⁺, Al³⁺, NH₄⁺ ...) aur negative charge wale (Cl⁻, O²⁻, SO₄²⁻, PO₄³⁻ ...). Ek baat bhi pakki hui thi: **charge aur valency ek hi number hain**. Ab sawal ye hai ki in tukdon ko jod kar kisi compound ka **poora formula** kaise likhein? Kitne Na⁺ ek SO₄²⁻ ke saath aayenge? Aaj ek chhoti si chaal (criss-cross) seekhenge jisse koi bhi formula 30 second mein ban jaata hai, aur phir ulta kaam bhi: formula dekh kar naam likhna."
