            "heading": "Part A: Atomic number Z, tatva ki pehchaan",
            "headingHinglish": "Part A: Atomic number Z, tatva ki pehchaan",
            "body": "**Atomic number (Z) = atom ke nucleus mein protons ki ginti.**\n\nYahi sankhya tay karti hai ki wo atom kaunse tatva ka hai:\n\n- Jis atom mein **1 proton** hai, wo hamesha hydrogen hai.\n- Jis atom mein **6 protons** hain, wo hamesha carbon hai.\n- Jis atom mein **11 protons** hain, wo hamesha sodium hai.\n\nNeutron ya electron badal jaayein to bhi tatva wahi rehta hai jab tak protons wahi hain. Par agar protons ki ginti badal jaaye, to **tatva hi badal jaata hai**. Isiliye Z ko tatva ka \"roll number\" kehte hain.\n\nEk zaroori baat: **neutral atom** mein protons positive hain aur electrons negative, aur dono barabar hote hain, isliye kul charge shunya (0) hota hai (Topic 1 ka wahi hisaab, aur charge ke baare mein Physics ke [Electricity](../../physics/electricity/electricity.md) chapter mein padha tha). Isse:\n\n**Neutral atom mein electrons ki ginti = protons ki ginti = Z**\n\n### Example 1. Hydrogen, carbon aur sodium ke Z\n\nHydrogen: 1 proton, to Z = 1, aur neutral atom mein 1 electron.\nCarbon: 6 protons, to Z = 6, aur 6 electrons.\nSodium: 11 protons, to Z = 11, aur 11 electrons.\n\nJaanch: neutral mein protons = electrons: 1 = 1, 6 = 6, 11 = 11 ✅",
            "bodyHinglish": "**Atomic number (Z) = atom ke nucleus mein protons ki ginti.**\n\nYahi sankhya tay karti hai ki wo atom kaunse tatva ka hai:\n\n- Jis atom mein **1 proton** hai, wo hamesha hydrogen hai.\n- Jis atom mein **6 protons** hain, wo hamesha carbon hai.\n- Jis atom mein **11 protons** hain, wo hamesha sodium hai.\n\nNeutron ya electron badal jaayein to bhi tatva wahi rehta hai jab tak protons wahi hain. Par agar protons ki ginti badal jaaye, to **tatva hi badal jaata hai**. Isiliye Z ko tatva ka \"roll number\" kehte hain.\n\nEk zaroori baat: **neutral atom** mein protons positive hain aur electrons negative, aur dono barabar hote hain, isliye kul charge shunya (0) hota hai (Topic 1 ka wahi hisaab, aur charge ke baare mein Physics ke [Electricity](../../physics/electricity/electricity.md) chapter mein padha tha). Isse:\n\n**Neutral atom mein electrons ki ginti = protons ki ginti = Z**\n\n### Example 1. Hydrogen, carbon aur sodium ke Z\n\nHydrogen: 1 proton, to Z = 1, aur neutral atom mein 1 electron.\nCarbon: 6 protons, to Z = 6, aur 6 electrons.\nSodium: 11 protons, to Z = 11, aur 11 electrons.\n\nJaanch: neutral mein protons = electrons: 1 = 1, 6 = 6, 11 = 11 ✅"
