            "headingHinglish": "Part A: Pehle ek bahut zaroori tasveer",
            "body": "Is poore topic ki chaabi ek hi hai. Do tarah ke attraction (aakarshan) hote hain, aur bahut alag-alag taakat ke:\n\n- **Ionic compound:** Na⁺ aur Cl⁻ jaise ions ke beech attraction hota hai. Ye attraction **positive aur negative charge** ka hai, bahut **strong**, aur ye poore crystal lattice mein **har ion ko chaaron taraf** se pakde rehta hai (Topic 2 ka lattice yaad karo: har Na⁺ ko 6 Cl⁻ ghere hue the).\n- **Covalent compound:** Ek molecule ke **andar** ka bond (shared electrons) to strong hota hai. Lekin ek molecule aur doosre molecule ke **beech** ka attraction (Chapter 1 wala aakarshan) bahut **kamzor** hota hai.\n\nYaad rakho, covalent compound ko pighlane ya ubalne mein molecule ke andar ka bond **nahi todna** padta. Bas ek molecule ko doosre se alag karna padta hai, jo aasan hai.\n\nEk ghar ki upma: ionic compound ek **kasi hui deewar** jaisa hai jisme har eent seedhe cement se jodi gayi hai. Covalent compound **gattha (cartons) ke dher** jaisa hai: har gattha khud mazboot hai, par gatthe ek doosre se sirf halke se rakhe hain.\n\nAage har gun mein hum isi tasveer ko lagayenge.",
