          {
            "heading": "Part D: Solved examples: decomposition",
            "headingHinglish": "Part D: Solved examples: decomposition",
            "body": "### Example 4. Limestone se kitna quicklime milta hai?\n\nMasses: Ca = 40, C = 12, O = 16. CaCO₃ ka mass = 40 + 12 + 16 × 3 = **100**. CaO ka mass = 40 + 16 = **56**. CO₂ ka mass = 12 + 32 = **44**.\n\nJaanch: 100 = 56 + 44 ✅. To **100 kg** shuddh limestone se **56 kg** quicklime aur **44 kg** CO₂ gas. To **1 tonne** (1000 kg) shuddh limestone se **560 kg** quicklime banta hai. Jo mass \"gayab\" hua wo CO₂ ke roop mein hawa mein chala gaya, jaisa Chapter 4 mein dekha tha.\n\n### Example 5. Baking soda ka hisaab\n\n2NaHCO₃ → Na₂CO₃ + H₂O + CO₂. Masses: Na = 23, H = 1, C = 12, O = 16. NaHCO₃ = 23 + 1 + 12 + 48 = **84**. 2 × 84 = **168**.\n\nDaayein: Na₂CO₃ = 46 + 12 + 48 = **106**. H₂O = **18**. CO₂ = **44**. Total = 106 + 18 + 44 = **168**.\n\nJaanch: 168 = 168 ✅. Ye mass bachne (Chapter 4) ka ek aur saboot hai.\n\n### Example 6. Kaun sa flavour hai?\n\nNeeche diye reactions mein flavour pehchano:\n- (i) Oven mein 2NaHCO₃ → Na₂CO₃ + H₂O + CO₂: **garmi** se, thermal.\n- (ii) Battery se paani ke electrode par 2H₂O → 2H₂ + O₂: **bijli** se, electrolytic.\n- (iii) Film par 2AgBr → 2Ag + Br₂: **roshni** se, photolytic.\n- (iv) Yeast ke saath 2H₂O₂ → 2H₂O + O₂: **catalyst** ki madad se.\n\nSab mein **ek hi reactant**, to sab decomposition hain. Sawal poochho: arrow ke baayein kitne formula? Agar **ek** hai, to decomposition ki sambhavna.",
            "bodyHinglish": "### Example 4. Limestone se kitna quicklime milta hai?\n\nMasses: Ca = 40, C = 12, O = 16. CaCO₃ ka mass = 40 + 12 + 16 × 3 = **100**. CaO ka mass = 40 + 16 = **56**. CO₂ ka mass = 12 + 32 = **44**.\n\nJaanch: 100 = 56 + 44 ✅. To **100 kg** shuddh limestone se **56 kg** quicklime aur **44 kg** CO₂ gas. To **1 tonne** (1000 kg) shuddh limestone se **560 kg** quicklime banta hai. Jo mass \"gayab\" hua wo CO₂ ke roop mein hawa mein chala gaya, jaisa Chapter 4 mein dekha tha.\n\n### Example 5. Baking soda ka hisaab\n\n2NaHCO₃ → Na₂CO₃ + H₂O + CO₂. Masses: Na = 23, H = 1, C = 12, O = 16. NaHCO₃ = 23 + 1 + 12 + 48 = **84**. 2 × 84 = **168**.\n\nDaayein: Na₂CO₃ = 46 + 12 + 48 = **106**. H₂O = **18**. CO₂ = **44**. Total = 106 + 18 + 44 = **168**.\n\nJaanch: 168 = 168 ✅. Ye mass bachne (Chapter 4) ka ek aur saboot hai.\n\n### Example 6. Kaun sa flavour hai?\n\nNeeche diye reactions mein flavour pehchano:\n- (i) Oven mein 2NaHCO₃ → Na₂CO₃ + H₂O + CO₂: **garmi** se, thermal.\n- (ii) Battery se paani ke electrode par 2H₂O → 2H₂ + O₂: **bijli** se, electrolytic.\n- (iii) Film par 2AgBr → 2Ag + Br₂: **roshni** se, photolytic.\n- (iv) Yeast ke saath 2H₂O₂ → 2H₂O + O₂: **catalyst** ki madad se.\n\nSab mein **ek hi reactant**, to sab decomposition hain. Sawal poochho: arrow ke baayein kitne formula? Agar **ek** hai, to decomposition ki sambhavna."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Part E: Ek sikke ke do pehlu",
            "headingHinglish": "Part E: Ek sikke ke do pehlu",
            "body": "Combination aur decomposition ek doosre ke **ulte** lagte hain. Aap ek hi reaction ko do dishaon mein dekho:\n\n| Jodna (combination) | Todna (decomposition) |\n|---|---|\n| 2H₂ + O₂ → 2H₂O (hydrogen jalna) | 2H₂O → 2H₂ + O₂ (bijli se) |\n| CaO + CO₂ → CaCO₃ (nayi chattan ban-ti hai) | CaCO₃ → CaO + CO₂ (kiln mein garmi se) |\n\nEk baat dhyan se: dono dishaon mein **atoms wahi hain**, bas unke saathi badal gaye. Iska matlab ye nahi ki ulta reaction **aise hi** shuru ho jaata hai. Har dishaa ke liye alag **shart** chahiye: ek ke liye 900 °C garmi, doosre ke liye hawa mein dheere-dheere. Aur energy ke hisaab se bhi dono ulte hain: jo reaction garmi bahar deta hai, uska ulta garmi leta hai. Ye hum Topic 4 mein dekhenge.\n\nPehchaan ka niyam yaad rakho:\n\n- **A + B → AB**: arrow ke daayein **ek** formula = combination.\n- **AB → A + B**: arrow ke baayein **ek** formula = decomposition.",
            "bodyHinglish": "Combination aur decomposition ek doosre ke **ulte** lagte hain. Aap ek hi reaction ko do dishaon mein dekho:\n\n| Jodna (combination) | Todna (decomposition) |\n|---|---|\n| 2H₂ + O₂ → 2H₂O (hydrogen jalna) | 2H₂O → 2H₂ + O₂ (bijli se) |\n| CaO + CO₂ → CaCO₃ (nayi chattan ban-ti hai) | CaCO₃ → CaO + CO₂ (kiln mein garmi se) |\n\nEk baat dhyan se: dono dishaon mein **atoms wahi hain**, bas unke saathi badal gaye. Iska matlab ye nahi ki ulta reaction **aise hi** shuru ho jaata hai. Har dishaa ke liye alag **shart** chahiye: ek ke liye 900 °C garmi, doosre ke liye hawa mein dheere-dheere. Aur energy ke hisaab se bhi dono ulte hain: jo reaction garmi bahar deta hai, uska ulta garmi leta hai. Ye hum Topic 4 mein dekhenge.\n\nPehchaan ka niyam yaad rakho:\n\n- **A + B → AB**: arrow ke daayein **ek** formula = combination.\n- **AB → A + B**: arrow ke baayein **ek** formula = decomposition."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Part F: Lime ki poori kahani: bhatti se deewar tak",
            "headingHinglish": "Part F: Lime ki poori kahani: bhatti se deewar tak",
            "body": "Ab bakery wale mazdoor ki balti ko poori kahani ke saath jodte hain. Chuna ek **ghoomta chakra** hai, jisme **decomposition aur combination dono** aate hain.\n\n```\n   LIMESTONE (CaCO₃)            \"chuna-patthar\", khan se\n        │\n        │  lime kiln mein garmi ~900 °C         (decomposition)\n        │  CaCO₃ ──► CaO + CO₂↑\n        ▼\n   QUICKLIME (CaO)              safed patthar, kostik: sirf adult ke saath\n        │\n        │  paani milao, bahut garmi nikalti hai (combination)\n        │  CaO + H₂O ──► Ca(OH)₂\n        ▼\n   SLAKED LIME (Ca(OH)₂)        whitewash ka ghol: deewar par lagaya jaata hai\n        │\n        │  deewar par sookhne ke baad dheere-dheere hawa ki CO₂ se\n        │  Ca(OH)₂ + CO₂ ──► CaCO₃ + H₂O        (teesra reaction: do products, combination nahi)\n        ▼\n   CaCO₃ ki patli parat         deewar par safed chamak, wapas limestone jaisi\n```\n\n> **Figure 2.3** – Lime ki kahani: limestone (CaCO₃) garmi se toot kar quicklime (CaO) aur CO₂ deta hai. Quicklime paani se mil kar slaked lime (Ca(OH)₂) banata hai. Whitewash sookhne par hawa ki CO₂ lekar wapas CaCO₃ ki parat ban jaati hai. Is chakra mein ek decomposition, ek combination aur ek teesra reaction aaya.\n\nYe Diwali se pehle ghar ki deewarein safed karne ki kahani bhi hai: chuna lagao, sookhne do, aur kuch dinon mein deewar par ek safed, thodi chamakti parat ban jaati hai. Uski wajah **hawa ki CO₂** hai.\n\nLast wale reaction ki jaanch: **Ca(OH)₂ + CO₂ → CaCO₃ + H₂O**. Ca: 1 = 1 ✅, C: 1 = 1 ✅, O: 2 + 2 = 4 aur 3 + 1 = 4 ✅, H: 2 = 2 ✅. (Is reaction mein product do hain, to ye strictly combination nahi hai. Isse bas \"ek aur reaction\" samjho; iske jaise reactions ka type tum aage seekhoge.)",
            "bodyHinglish": "Ab bakery wale mazdoor ki balti ko poori kahani ke saath jodte hain. Chuna ek **ghoomta chakra** hai, jisme **decomposition aur combination dono** aate hain.\n\n```\n   LIMESTONE (CaCO₃)            \"chuna-patthar\", khan se\n        │\n        │  lime kiln mein garmi ~900 °C         (decomposition)\n        │  CaCO₃ ──► CaO + CO₂↑\n        ▼\n   QUICKLIME (CaO)              safed patthar, kostik: sirf adult ke saath\n        │\n        │  paani milao, bahut garmi nikalti hai (combination)\n        │  CaO + H₂O ──► Ca(OH)₂\n        ▼\n   SLAKED LIME (Ca(OH)₂)        whitewash ka ghol: deewar par lagaya jaata hai\n        │\n        │  deewar par sookhne ke baad dheere-dheere hawa ki CO₂ se\n        │  Ca(OH)₂ + CO₂ ──► CaCO₃ + H₂O        (teesra reaction: do products, combination nahi)\n        ▼\n   CaCO₃ ki patli parat         deewar par safed chamak, wapas limestone jaisi\n```\n\n> **Figure 2.3** – Lime ki kahani: limestone (CaCO₃) garmi se toot kar quicklime (CaO) aur CO₂ deta hai. Quicklime paani se mil kar slaked lime (Ca(OH)₂) banata hai. Whitewash sookhne par hawa ki CO₂ lekar wapas CaCO₃ ki parat ban jaati hai. Is chakra mein ek decomposition, ek combination aur ek teesra reaction aaya.\n\nYe Diwali se pehle ghar ki deewarein safed karne ki kahani bhi hai: chuna lagao, sookhne do, aur kuch dinon mein deewar par ek safed, thodi chamakti parat ban jaati hai. Uski wajah **hawa ki CO₂** hai.\n\nLast wale reaction ki jaanch: **Ca(OH)₂ + CO₂ → CaCO₃ + H₂O**. Ca: 1 = 1 ✅, C: 1 = 1 ✅, O: 2 + 2 = 4 aur 3 + 1 = 4 ✅, H: 2 = 2 ✅. (Is reaction mein product do hain, to ye strictly combination nahi hai. Isse bas \"ek aur reaction\" samjho; iske jaise reactions ka type tum aage seekhoge.)"
          },
          {
            "heading": "Part G: Balancing practice",
            "headingHinglish": "Part G: Balancing practice",
            "body": "Chapter 3 ke Topic 6 wala hit-and-trial yaad rakho: pehle **formula**, phir **coefficient**, aur aakhir mein har atom ki ginti.\n\n### Example 7. Mg + O₂ → MgO\n\nBaayein Mg = 1, O = 2. Daayein Mg = 1, O = 1. O barabar karne ke liye 2MgO: ab daayein Mg = 2, O = 2. Baayein Mg ko 2 karo: **2Mg + O₂ → 2MgO**.\n\nJaanch: Mg: 2 = 2 ✅, O: 2 = 2 ✅.\n\n### Example 8. NaHCO₃ → Na₂CO₃ + H₂O + CO₂\n\nDaayein Na = 2, to baayein 2NaHCO₃. Ab baayein Na = 2, H = 2, C = 2, O = 6. Daayein: Na = 2, H = 2, C = 1 + 1 = 2, O = 3 + 1 + 2 = 6. **2NaHCO₃ → Na₂CO₃ + H₂O + CO₂**.\n\nJaanch: Na: 2 = 2 ✅, H: 2 = 2 ✅, C: 2 = 2 ✅, O: 6 = 6 ✅.\n\n### Example 9. H₂O₂ → H₂O + O₂\n\nBaayein H = 2, O = 2. Daayein H = 2, O = 1 + 2 = 3. O ka hisaab bigda. O₂ aur H₂O₂ mein O ki ginti 2 ke gunak mein aati hai, to 2H₂O₂ lo: baayein H = 4, O = 4. Daayein 2H₂O (H = 4, O = 2) aur O₂ (O = 2): **2H₂O₂ → 2H₂O + O₂**.\n\nJaanch: H: 4 = 4 ✅, O: 4 = 2 + 2 = 4 ✅.",
            "bodyHinglish": "Chapter 3 ke Topic 6 wala hit-and-trial yaad rakho: pehle **formula**, phir **coefficient**, aur aakhir mein har atom ki ginti.\n\n### Example 7. Mg + O₂ → MgO\n\nBaayein Mg = 1, O = 2. Daayein Mg = 1, O = 1. O barabar karne ke liye 2MgO: ab daayein Mg = 2, O = 2. Baayein Mg ko 2 karo: **2Mg + O₂ → 2MgO**.\n\nJaanch: Mg: 2 = 2 ✅, O: 2 = 2 ✅.\n\n### Example 8. NaHCO₃ → Na₂CO₃ + H₂O + CO₂\n\nDaayein Na = 2, to baayein 2NaHCO₃. Ab baayein Na = 2, H = 2, C = 2, O = 6. Daayein: Na = 2, H = 2, C = 1 + 1 = 2, O = 3 + 1 + 2 = 6. **2NaHCO₃ → Na₂CO₃ + H₂O + CO₂**.\n\nJaanch: Na: 2 = 2 ✅, H: 2 = 2 ✅, C: 2 = 2 ✅, O: 6 = 6 ✅.\n\n### Example 9. H₂O₂ → H₂O + O₂\n\nBaayein H = 2, O = 2. Daayein H = 2, O = 1 + 2 = 3. O ka hisaab bigda. O₂ aur H₂O₂ mein O ki ginti 2 ke gunak mein aati hai, to 2H₂O₂ lo: baayein H = 4, O = 4. Daayein 2H₂O (H = 4, O = 2) aur O₂ (O = 2): **2H₂O₂ → 2H₂O + O₂**.\n\nJaanch: H: 4 = 4 ✅, O: 4 = 2 + 2 = 4 ✅."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Aam galtiyan (bachke rehna)",
            "headingHinglish": "Aam galtiyan (bachke rehna)",
            "body": "**Galti 1: Combination ko \"do cheezein mili\" tak hi samajhna**\n\nC + O₂ → CO₂ aur CH₄ + 2O₂ → CO₂ + 2H₂O, dono mein do reactant hain. Par pehla combination hai (ek product), doosra nahi (do products). Reactants nahi, **product ki ginti** dekho.\n\n**Galti 2: Decomposition ko \"sirf garmi se tootna\" samajhna**\n\nTeen flavour hain: garmi, bijli, roshni. Baking soda aur limestone garmi se, paani bijli se, AgBr roshni se. Catalyst wala bhi hota hai.\n\n**Galti 3: Chuna haath se chhoona**\n\nQuicklime aur slaked lime kostik hote hain. Sirf adult dastaane aur chashme ke saath sambhalte hain. Tum bas door se samjho.\n\n**Galti 4: Band tube ya bottle mein gas banne wala reaction karna**\n\nCO₂ ya O₂ banne wale reaction band bottle ya tube mein **kabhi** na karo: andar dabav badhta hai aur wo fat sakta hai. Hamesha khula rakho.\n\n**Galti 5: Mass \"gayab\" ho jaata hai**\n\nLimestone garam karne par jo patthar bacha wo halka hai (100 se 56). Par CO₂ gas bahar chali gayi (44). Total hamesha same: 56 + 44 = 100.",
            "bodyHinglish": "**Galti 1: Combination ko \"do cheezein mili\" tak hi samajhna**\n\nC + O₂ → CO₂ aur CH₄ + 2O₂ → CO₂ + 2H₂O, dono mein do reactant hain. Par pehla combination hai (ek product), doosra nahi (do products). Reactants nahi, **product ki ginti** dekho.\n\n**Galti 2: Decomposition ko \"sirf garmi se tootna\" samajhna**\n\nTeen flavour hain: garmi, bijli, roshni. Baking soda aur limestone garmi se, paani bijli se, AgBr roshni se. Catalyst wala bhi hota hai.\n\n**Galti 3: Chuna haath se chhoona**\n\nQuicklime aur slaked lime kostik hote hain. Sirf adult dastaane aur chashme ke saath sambhalte hain. Tum bas door se samjho.\n\n**Galti 4: Band tube ya bottle mein gas banne wala reaction karna**\n\nCO₂ ya O₂ banne wale reaction band bottle ya tube mein **kabhi** na karo: andar dabav badhta hai aur wo fat sakta hai. Hamesha khula rakho.\n\n**Galti 5: Mass \"gayab\" ho jaata hai**\n\nLimestone garam karne par jo patthar bacha wo halka hai (100 se 56). Par CO₂ gas bahar chali gayi (44). Total hamesha same: 56 + 44 = 100."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Quick Recap",
            "headingHinglish": "Quick Recap",
            "body": "- **Combination:** do ya zyada reactants mil kar **ek hi product**. A + B → AB. Udaharan: 2Mg + O₂ → 2MgO, C + O₂ → CO₂, 2H₂ + O₂ → 2H₂O, N₂ + 3H₂ → 2NH₃, CaO + H₂O → Ca(OH)₂.\n- **Decomposition:** **ek reactant** toot kar do ya zyada simple products. AB → A + B.\n- Decomposition ke flavour: **garmi** (CaCO₃, NaHCO₃), **bijli** (2H₂O → 2H₂ + O₂), **roshni** (2AgBr → 2Ag + Br₂), aur **catalyst** (2H₂O₂ → 2H₂O + O₂).\n- Dono ek doosre ke ulte hain, par ulta reaction apni alag shart (garmi, bijli) maangta hai.\n- Lime ki kahani: CaCO₃ → CaO + CO₂ (kiln), CaO + H₂O → Ca(OH)₂ (slaking), phir deewar par CO₂ se wapas CaCO₃.\n- Quicklime kostik hai: sirf adult ke saath; students nahi chhuenge. Gas banne wale reaction **band** container mein kabhi nahi.\n- Teeno mein mass dono taraf barabar: 100 = 56 + 44, 168 = 106 + 18 + 44.",
            "bodyHinglish": "- **Combination:** do ya zyada reactants mil kar **ek hi product**. A + B → AB. Udaharan: 2Mg + O₂ → 2MgO, C + O₂ → CO₂, 2H₂ + O₂ → 2H₂O, N₂ + 3H₂ → 2NH₃, CaO + H₂O → Ca(OH)₂.\n- **Decomposition:** **ek reactant** toot kar do ya zyada simple products. AB → A + B.\n- Decomposition ke flavour: **garmi** (CaCO₃, NaHCO₃), **bijli** (2H₂O → 2H₂ + O₂), **roshni** (2AgBr → 2Ag + Br₂), aur **catalyst** (2H₂O₂ → 2H₂O + O₂).\n- Dono ek doosre ke ulte hain, par ulta reaction apni alag shart (garmi, bijli) maangta hai.\n- Lime ki kahani: CaCO₃ → CaO + CO₂ (kiln), CaO + H₂O → Ca(OH)₂ (slaking), phir deewar par CO₂ se wapas CaCO₃.\n- Quicklime kostik hai: sirf adult ke saath; students nahi chhuenge. Gas banne wale reaction **band** container mein kabhi nahi.\n- Teeno mein mass dono taraf barabar: 100 = 56 + 44, 168 = 106 + 18 + 44."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Practice Questions",
            "headingHinglish": "Practice Questions",
            "body": "1. Define a combination reaction and a decomposition reaction in your own words. Give one example of each with a balanced equation.\n\n2. Look at the equation CH₄ + 2O₂ → CO₂ + 2H₂O. Is it a combination reaction? Give a reason using the number of products.\n\n3. Balance each equation and verify by counting atoms. Say whether each is combination or decomposition: (a) Ca + O₂ → CaO (b) KClO₃ → KCl + O₂ (c) Na + Cl₂ → NaCl (d) N₂ + H₂ → NH₃.\n\n4. Why does a cake rise when baking soda is added to the batter and baked? Write the equation of the reaction and name the gas.\n\n5. Name the three main ways to decompose a compound. Give one example for each, with its balanced equation, and say which one is used in old black-and-white photographic film.\n\n6. Calculate how much quicklime and how much carbon dioxide you get by heating 500 kg of pure limestone (Ca = 40, C = 12, O = 16). Check that the masses add up.\n\n7. When water is decomposed by electric current, 2H₂O → 2H₂ + O₂, how do the volumes of hydrogen and oxygen compare? Explain using the equation.\n\n8. Write the story of lime in order: limestone, quicklime, slaked lime, and back to limestone. Which steps are decomposition and which are combination?\n\n9. State True or False and correct the false ones:\n   (a) In a combination reaction, the product is always one substance.\n   (b) A decomposition reaction needs two reactants.\n   (c) Quicklime is safe to touch with bare hands.\n   (d) It is safe to heat baking soda in a tightly closed test tube.\n\n10. Classify each of the following as combination or decomposition, and explain: (a) 2H₂ + O₂ → 2H₂O (b) CaCO₃ → CaO + CO₂ (c) CaO + H₂O → Ca(OH)₂ (d) 2AgBr → 2Ag + Br₂ (e) C + O₂ → CO₂.\n\n11. Two reactions look like opposites: 2H₂ + O₂ → 2H₂O and 2H₂O → 2H₂ + O₂. In what two ways are they the same, and in what way are they different?\n\n### Answers\n\n1. **Combination:** do ya zyada reactants mil kar **ek hi product** banate hain, jaise 2Mg + O₂ → 2MgO (Mg: 2 = 2 ✅, O: 2 = 2 ✅). **Decomposition:** **ek reactant** toot kar do ya zyada products banata hai, jaise CaCO₃ → CaO + CO₂ (Ca 1 = 1 ✅, C 1 = 1 ✅, O 3 = 3 ✅).\n\n2. **Nahi.** Isme do products hain (CO₂ aur H₂O). Combination mein arrow ke daayein sirf **ek** formula hota hai. Ye combustion hai, jo Topic 6 mein aayega.\n\n3. (a) **2Ca + O₂ → 2CaO** (combination): Ca 2 = 2 ✅, O 2 = 2 ✅. (b) **2KClO₃ → 2KCl + 3O₂** (decomposition): K 2 = 2 ✅, Cl 2 = 2 ✅, O 6 = 3 × 2 = 6 ✅. Yahan O pehle 3 aur 2 ke beech atka tha, isliye 6 tak le gaye. (c) **2Na + Cl₂ → 2NaCl** (combination): Na 2 = 2 ✅, Cl 2 = 2 ✅. (d) **N₂ + 3H₂ → 2NH₃** (combination): N 2 = 2 ✅, H 6 = 6 ✅.\n\n4. Baking soda garam oven mein toot-ta hai: **2NaHCO₃ → Na₂CO₃ + H₂O + CO₂**. **CO₂** gas ke bubbles ghol mein bante hain aur cake ko phoola dete hain. Ye thermal decomposition hai.\n\n5. Garmi (thermal): **CaCO₃ → CaO + CO₂**. Bijli (electrolytic): **2H₂O → 2H₂ + O₂**. Roshni (photolytic): **2AgBr → 2Ag + Br₂**; ye black-and-white film mein hota tha. Teeno equations balanced hain: Ca/C/O 1,1,3 = 1,1,3 ✅; H/O 4,2 = 4,2 ✅; Ag/Br 2,2 = 2,2 ✅.\n\n6. CaCO₃ = 100, CaO = 56, CO₂ = 44, to 100 : 56 : 44. 500 kg ke liye 5 guna: **quicklime = 5 × 56 = 280 kg**, **CO₂ = 5 × 44 = 220 kg**. Jaanch: 280 + 220 = 500 ✅.\n\n7. **Hydrogen ka volume oxygen se do guna** hota hai, kyunki equation mein 2 molecule H₂ aur sirf 1 molecule O₂ hai (ek hi garmi aur dabav par gas ka volume molecules ki ginti ke saath chalta hai; iska kaaran aage ki class mein). Jaanch: H: 4 = 4 ✅, O: 2 = 2 ✅.\n\n8. Limestone (CaCO₃) → garmi se quicklime (CaO) + CO₂: **decomposition**. Quicklime + paani → slaked lime (Ca(OH)₂): **combination**. Whitewash sookhne par hawa ki CO₂ se wapas CaCO₃: **Ca(OH)₂ + CO₂ → CaCO₃ + H₂O** (Ca 1 = 1 ✅, C 1 = 1 ✅, O 4 = 4 ✅, H 2 = 2 ✅). Ye do products wala reaction hai, to strictly combination nahi.\n\n9. (a) **True** ✅. (b) **False** ❌. Decomposition mein **ek** reactant hota hai. (c) **False** ❌. Quicklime kostik hai, sirf adult dastaane aur chashme ke saath. (d) **False** ❌. Band tube mein gas bharne se wo fat sakta hai; tube khula rehna chahiye.\n\n10. (a) **Combination** (do reactants, ek product). (b) **Decomposition** (ek reactant, do products). (c) **Combination** (do reactants, ek product). (d) **Decomposition** (ek reactant, do products). (e) **Combination** (do reactants, ek product).\n\n11. Dono mein **wahi atoms** hain (H = 4, O = 2 dono taraf) aur dono mein bond todke naye jodte hain. Farq ye hai ki pehla **combination** hai (hydrogen jalna, garmi bahar nikalti hai), aur doosra **decomposition** hai jisme **bijli** deni padti hai.\n\n---\n\nShabaash! Ab tumhe pata hai ki bakery mein cake kaise phoola aur balti ka chuna kahan se aaya. Combination mein cheezein judti hain, decomposition mein toot-ti hain, aur donon mein atoms ki ginti kabhi nahi badalti.\n\n**Aage kya?** Aaj tak ke reactions mein ya to cheezein mili thi ya ek toot gayi thi. Lekin ek aur tarah ka reaction hai jisme ek **atom doosre ko uski jagah se bahar nikaal deta hai**. Agle topic **\"Displacement aur Double Displacement\"** mein ek lohe ki keel neele ghol mein daalenge, aur dekhenge ki kaun kise kyun nikaalta hai.",
            "bodyHinglish": "1. Define a combination reaction and a decomposition reaction in your own words. Give one example of each with a balanced equation.\n\n2. Look at the equation CH₄ + 2O₂ → CO₂ + 2H₂O. Is it a combination reaction? Give a reason using the number of products.\n\n3. Balance each equation and verify by counting atoms. Say whether each is combination or decomposition: (a) Ca + O₂ → CaO (b) KClO₃ → KCl + O₂ (c) Na + Cl₂ → NaCl (d) N₂ + H₂ → NH₃.\n\n4. Why does a cake rise when baking soda is added to the batter and baked? Write the equation of the reaction and name the gas.\n\n5. Name the three main ways to decompose a compound. Give one example for each, with its balanced equation, and say which one is used in old black-and-white photographic film.\n\n6. Calculate how much quicklime and how much carbon dioxide you get by heating 500 kg of pure limestone (Ca = 40, C = 12, O = 16). Check that the masses add up.\n\n7. When water is decomposed by electric current, 2H₂O → 2H₂ + O₂, how do the volumes of hydrogen and oxygen compare? Explain using the equation.\n\n8. Write the story of lime in order: limestone, quicklime, slaked lime, and back to limestone. Which steps are decomposition and which are combination?\n\n9. State True or False and correct the false ones:\n   (a) In a combination reaction, the product is always one substance.\n   (b) A decomposition reaction needs two reactants.\n   (c) Quicklime is safe to touch with bare hands.\n   (d) It is safe to heat baking soda in a tightly closed test tube.\n\n10. Classify each of the following as combination or decomposition, and explain: (a) 2H₂ + O₂ → 2H₂O (b) CaCO₃ → CaO + CO₂ (c) CaO + H₂O → Ca(OH)₂ (d) 2AgBr → 2Ag + Br₂ (e) C + O₂ → CO₂.\n\n11. Two reactions look like opposites: 2H₂ + O₂ → 2H₂O and 2H₂O → 2H₂ + O₂. In what two ways are they the same, and in what way are they different?\n\n### Answers\n\n1. **Combination:** do ya zyada reactants mil kar **ek hi product** banate hain, jaise 2Mg + O₂ → 2MgO (Mg: 2 = 2 ✅, O: 2 = 2 ✅). **Decomposition:** **ek reactant** toot kar do ya zyada products banata hai, jaise CaCO₃ → CaO + CO₂ (Ca 1 = 1 ✅, C 1 = 1 ✅, O 3 = 3 ✅).\n\n2. **Nahi.** Isme do products hain (CO₂ aur H₂O). Combination mein arrow ke daayein sirf **ek** formula hota hai. Ye combustion hai, jo Topic 6 mein aayega.\n\n3. (a) **2Ca + O₂ → 2CaO** (combination): Ca 2 = 2 ✅, O 2 = 2 ✅. (b) **2KClO₃ → 2KCl + 3O₂** (decomposition): K 2 = 2 ✅, Cl 2 = 2 ✅, O 6 = 3 × 2 = 6 ✅. Yahan O pehle 3 aur 2 ke beech atka tha, isliye 6 tak le gaye. (c) **2Na + Cl₂ → 2NaCl** (combination): Na 2 = 2 ✅, Cl 2 = 2 ✅. (d) **N₂ + 3H₂ → 2NH₃** (combination): N 2 = 2 ✅, H 6 = 6 ✅.\n\n4. Baking soda garam oven mein toot-ta hai: **2NaHCO₃ → Na₂CO₃ + H₂O + CO₂**. **CO₂** gas ke bubbles ghol mein bante hain aur cake ko phoola dete hain. Ye thermal decomposition hai.\n\n5. Garmi (thermal): **CaCO₃ → CaO + CO₂**. Bijli (electrolytic): **2H₂O → 2H₂ + O₂**. Roshni (photolytic): **2AgBr → 2Ag + Br₂**; ye black-and-white film mein hota tha. Teeno equations balanced hain: Ca/C/O 1,1,3 = 1,1,3 ✅; H/O 4,2 = 4,2 ✅; Ag/Br 2,2 = 2,2 ✅.\n\n6. CaCO₃ = 100, CaO = 56, CO₂ = 44, to 100 : 56 : 44. 500 kg ke liye 5 guna: **quicklime = 5 × 56 = 280 kg**, **CO₂ = 5 × 44 = 220 kg**. Jaanch: 280 + 220 = 500 ✅.\n\n7. **Hydrogen ka volume oxygen se do guna** hota hai, kyunki equation mein 2 molecule H₂ aur sirf 1 molecule O₂ hai (ek hi garmi aur dabav par gas ka volume molecules ki ginti ke saath chalta hai; iska kaaran aage ki class mein). Jaanch: H: 4 = 4 ✅, O: 2 = 2 ✅.\n\n8. Limestone (CaCO₃) → garmi se quicklime (CaO) + CO₂: **decomposition**. Quicklime + paani → slaked lime (Ca(OH)₂): **combination**. Whitewash sookhne par hawa ki CO₂ se wapas CaCO₃: **Ca(OH)₂ + CO₂ → CaCO₃ + H₂O** (Ca 1 = 1 ✅, C 1 = 1 ✅, O 4 = 4 ✅, H 2 = 2 ✅). Ye do products wala reaction hai, to strictly combination nahi.\n\n9. (a) **True** ✅. (b) **False** ❌. Decomposition mein **ek** reactant hota hai. (c) **False** ❌. Quicklime kostik hai, sirf adult dastaane aur chashme ke saath. (d) **False** ❌. Band tube mein gas bharne se wo fat sakta hai; tube khula rehna chahiye.\n\n10. (a) **Combination** (do reactants, ek product). (b) **Decomposition** (ek reactant, do products). (c) **Combination** (do reactants, ek product). (d) **Decomposition** (ek reactant, do products). (e) **Combination** (do reactants, ek product).\n\n11. Dono mein **wahi atoms** hain (H = 4, O = 2 dono taraf) aur dono mein bond todke naye jodte hain. Farq ye hai ki pehla **combination** hai (hydrogen jalna, garmi bahar nikalti hai), aur doosra **decomposition** hai jisme **bijli** deni padti hai.\n\n---\n\nShabaash! Ab tumhe pata hai ki bakery mein cake kaise phoola aur balti ka chuna kahan se aaya. Combination mein cheezein judti hain, decomposition mein toot-ti hain, aur donon mein atoms ki ginti kabhi nahi badalti.\n\n**Aage kya?** Aaj tak ke reactions mein ya to cheezein mili thi ya ek toot gayi thi. Lekin ek aur tarah ka reaction hai jisme ek **atom doosre ko uski jagah se bahar nikaal deta hai**. Agle topic **\"Displacement aur Double Displacement\"** mein ek lohe ki keel neele ghol mein daalenge, aur dekhenge ki kaun kise kyun nikaalta hai."
          }
