            "heading": "Harmonium ki chaabiyan",
            "headingHinglish": "Harmonium ki chaabiyan",
            "body": "Mr. Karnik ke ghar ek purana harmonium rakha tha. Unki bhatiji Mitali ne ek din dhool jhaadkar uski chaabiyan dabayi: **Sa Re Ga Ma Pa Dha Ni**, aur phir agli chaabi par wahi **Sa** dobara sunai diya, bas thoda unchi awaaz mein. \"Chacha, ye kya? Naya swar aaya aur wahi purana sunai de raha hai!\"\n\nMr. Karnik hanse. \"Isse **saptak** kehte hain. Saat swar, aur aathvi chaabi par pehle swar jaisa hi swar aata hai, bas unchi pitch par. Isi ko **octave** bhi kehte hain, yaani 'aathva'. Harmonium par kitni bhi chaabiyan hon, har aathvi chaabi par wahi swabhav wapas aa jaata hai.\"\n\nMitali ne chaabiyan ginkar dekhi. \"Sa se shuru karun to Sa, Re, Ga, Ma, Pa, Dha, Ni, aur aathvi chaabi phir Sa. Sach mein! To kya chaabiyan ek order mein lagi hain aur har aathvi dohrati hai?\" Mr. Karnik ne kaha, \"Bilkul. Ab ek sawaal soch: agar tatvon ko bhi ek line mein sahi order mein rakhein, to kya unmein bhi aisa koi dohrana ho sakta hai? Kuch vaigyanikon ne yehi socha tha. Chalo, unki kahani dekhte hain: kahan unhe jeet mili aur kahan wo atak gaye.\"",
