            "headingHinglish": "Hotel ki floor aur room number",
            "body": "Mr. Gadgil apni bhatiji Pranjal ko ek hotel mein ek shaadi ke function mein le gaye. Reception par ek mehmaan ne poochha, \"Mehta ji kahan ruke hain?\" Receptionist ne register dekha aur kaha, \"Teesri **floor**, room number **17**.\"\n\nPranjal ne dekha ki mehmaan seedha lift mein gaya, teesri floor par utra, aur 17 number ke darwaze par pahunch gaya. Pranjal ne poochha, \"Chacha, sirf do number se poora pata mil gaya? Naam ya shakal nahi poochhi?\" Mr. Gadgil ne kaha, \"Haan, kyunki hotel mein **floor** batata hai ki 'kitna upar', aur **room number** batata hai ki 'floor par kahan'. Do number milke ek hi kamre ko pakad lete hain. Aur dhyan de: har floor par rooms ek hi tarah ginte hain, to **ek hi room number** wale kamre har floor par sidhi line mein ek ke upar ek hote hain.\"\n\nPranjal ne socha, \"Matlab kisi ko dhoondna ho, to bas do cheezein chahiye: floor aur room.\" Mr. Gadgil muskuraaye. \"Aaj wahi khel hum tatvon ke saath khelenge. Har tatva ka ek **period** (floor) aur ek **group** (room number) hoga, aur wo kisi bhi tatva ka pata bata dega. Aur bonus: ye do number tatva ke electrons se seedha nikalte hain.\"",
            "bodyHinglish": "Mr. Gadgil apni bhatiji Pranjal ko ek hotel mein ek shaadi ke function mein le gaye. Reception par ek mehmaan ne poochha, \"Mehta ji kahan ruke hain?\" Receptionist ne register dekha aur kaha, \"Teesri **floor**, room number **17**.\"\n\nPranjal ne dekha ki mehmaan seedha lift mein gaya, teesri floor par utra, aur 17 number ke darwaze par pahunch gaya. Pranjal ne poochha, \"Chacha, sirf do number se poora pata mil gaya? Naam ya shakal nahi poochhi?\" Mr. Gadgil ne kaha, \"Haan, kyunki hotel mein **floor** batata hai ki 'kitna upar', aur **room number** batata hai ki 'floor par kahan'. Do number milke ek hi kamre ko pakad lete hain. Aur dhyan de: har floor par rooms ek hi tarah ginte hain, to **ek hi room number** wale kamre har floor par sidhi line mein ek ke upar ek hote hain.\"\n\nPranjal ne socha, \"Matlab kisi ko dhoondna ho, to bas do cheezein chahiye: floor aur room.\" Mr. Gadgil muskuraaye. \"Aaj wahi khel hum tatvon ke saath khelenge. Har tatva ka ek **period** (floor) aur ek **group** (room number) hoga, aur wo kisi bhi tatva ka pata bata dega. Aur bonus: ye do number tatva ke electrons se seedha nikalte hain.\""
