          {
            "heading": "Part G: Kathor paani ke fayde (haan, hain)",
            "headingHinglish": "Part G: Kathor paani ke fayde (haan, hain)",
            "body": "Kathor paani ko \"bura\" kehna adhoora hoga:\n\n1. **Swaad:** kuch logon ko kathor paani ka swaad pasand aata hai, aur bahut mridu paani unhe \"feeka\" lagta hai. (Ye pasand ki baat hai; swaad jaanchne ke liye lab ka paani kabhi chakhna nahi.)\n2. **Calcium:** peene ke paani se hamein thoda calcium aur magnesium bhi milta hai, jo haddi aur sharir ke liye zaroori mineral hain (par bada hissa khane se milta hai, paani se nahi). Isliye kathor paani peene ke liye aam taur par theek mana jaata hai.\n\nAur ek baat: bahut mridu paani mein sabun aasani se dhulta nahi (haath der tak chikne lagte hain), isliye wahan thoda sabun hi kaafi hai.",
            "bodyHinglish": "Kathor paani ko \"bura\" kehna adhoora hoga:\n\n1. **Swaad:** kuch logon ko kathor paani ka swaad pasand aata hai, aur bahut mridu paani unhe \"feeka\" lagta hai. (Ye pasand ki baat hai; swaad jaanchne ke liye lab ka paani kabhi chakhna nahi.)\n2. **Calcium:** peene ke paani se hamein thoda calcium aur magnesium bhi milta hai, jo haddi aur sharir ke liye zaroori mineral hain (par bada hissa khane se milta hai, paani se nahi). Isliye kathor paani peene ke liye aam taur par theek mana jaata hai.\n\nAur ek baat: bahut mridu paani mein sabun aasani se dhulta nahi (haath der tak chikne lagte hain), isliye wahan thoda sabun hi kaafi hai."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Part H: Reasoning: socho aur batao",
            "headingHinglish": "Part H: Reasoning: socho aur batao",
            "body": "### Example 6. Paani ubalne par jhaag badha: iska matlab?\n\nEk student ne nal ke paani se sabun ka test kiya, phir usi paani ko ubaal kar thanda karke test kiya. Pehle **kam jhaag**, phir **zyada jhaag**.\n\n- Ubalne se kathorta **kam hui**, yaani **asthayi kathorta** thi, jo Ca(HCO₃)₂ aur Mg(HCO₃)₂ se thi.\n- Agar ubalne ke baad bhi jhaag **utna hi kam** rehta, to kathorta **sthayi** hoti (CaCl₂ ya MgSO₄ jaise salt).\n\n### Example 7. Do paani, ek hi nateeja?\n\nPaani P: ubalne ke baad **jhaag bahut badhta hai**. Paani Q: ubalne ke baad **jhaag bilkul nahi badhta**.\n\n- P mein **mostly asthayi** kathorta hai (hydrogencarbonate).\n- Q mein **mostly sthayi** kathorta hai (chloride aur sulphate), jo ubalne se nahi gayi.\n\n### Example 8. Kettle ka scale kya batata hai?\n\nMr. Phadke ka kettle saaf nahi hota. Agar scale **CaCO₃** hai, to iska seedha matlab: paani mein **Ca(HCO₃)₂** (asthayi) tha, kyunki CaCO₃ ubalne se hi banta hai. (Sthayi wale CaCl₂ ya CaSO₄ ubalne par CaCO₃ nahi dete. CaSO₄ ki bahut thodi sakht parat boiler mein bhi jam sakti hai, par ye aage ki baat hai.)\n\n### Example 9. Washing soda ko paani mein dalne ka asar\n\nKathor paani mein CaCl₂ ghula hai. Usme washing soda daalne par **dudhiya safed** thos banta hai, jo neeche baith jaata hai. Ye thos kya hai? **CaCO₃**: kyunki CaCl₂ + Na₂CO₃ → CaCO₃ + 2NaCl, aur CaCO₃ paani mein nahi ghulta. Upar ka saaf paani ab **mridu** hai.",
            "bodyHinglish": "### Example 6. Paani ubalne par jhaag badha: iska matlab?\n\nEk student ne nal ke paani se sabun ka test kiya, phir usi paani ko ubaal kar thanda karke test kiya. Pehle **kam jhaag**, phir **zyada jhaag**.\n\n- Ubalne se kathorta **kam hui**, yaani **asthayi kathorta** thi, jo Ca(HCO₃)₂ aur Mg(HCO₃)₂ se thi.\n- Agar ubalne ke baad bhi jhaag **utna hi kam** rehta, to kathorta **sthayi** hoti (CaCl₂ ya MgSO₄ jaise salt).\n\n### Example 7. Do paani, ek hi nateeja?\n\nPaani P: ubalne ke baad **jhaag bahut badhta hai**. Paani Q: ubalne ke baad **jhaag bilkul nahi badhta**.\n\n- P mein **mostly asthayi** kathorta hai (hydrogencarbonate).\n- Q mein **mostly sthayi** kathorta hai (chloride aur sulphate), jo ubalne se nahi gayi.\n\n### Example 8. Kettle ka scale kya batata hai?\n\nMr. Phadke ka kettle saaf nahi hota. Agar scale **CaCO₃** hai, to iska seedha matlab: paani mein **Ca(HCO₃)₂** (asthayi) tha, kyunki CaCO₃ ubalne se hi banta hai. (Sthayi wale CaCl₂ ya CaSO₄ ubalne par CaCO₃ nahi dete. CaSO₄ ki bahut thodi sakht parat boiler mein bhi jam sakti hai, par ye aage ki baat hai.)\n\n### Example 9. Washing soda ko paani mein dalne ka asar\n\nKathor paani mein CaCl₂ ghula hai. Usme washing soda daalne par **dudhiya safed** thos banta hai, jo neeche baith jaata hai. Ye thos kya hai? **CaCO₃**: kyunki CaCl₂ + Na₂CO₃ → CaCO₃ + 2NaCl, aur CaCO₃ paani mein nahi ghulta. Upar ka saaf paani ab **mridu** hai."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Aam galtiyan (bachke rehna)",
            "headingHinglish": "Aam galtiyan (bachke rehna)",
            "body": "**Galti 1: \"Kathor paani zeheela hota hai\"**\n\nNahi. Kathor paani mein calcium aur magnesium ke salt hote hain, jo aam taur par hanikarak nahi. Problem **sabun, kettle aur boiler** ki hai.\n\n**Galti 2: \"Ubalne se har tarah ka kathor paani mridu ho jaata hai\"**\n\nUbalne se **sirf asthayi** kathorta jaati hai. **Sthayi** kathorta (chloride aur sulphate wali) **nahi** jaati.\n\n**Galti 3: \"Kettle ka scale ek tarah ka zang ya mitti hai\"**\n\nNahi. Wo **CaCO₃** hai: Ca(HCO₃)₂ ke ubalne se bana thos. Zang loha par banta hai, ye alag cheez hai.\n\n**Galti 4: \"Washing soda paani ko bhaap bana deta hai\" ya \"sab ghula deta hai\"**\n\nWashing soda Ca²⁺ aur Mg²⁺ ko CaCO₃ aur MgCO₃ **thos** bana kar paani se **bahar** karta hai. Wo ghulte nahi, neeche baithte hain.\n\n**Galti 5: \"Sabun ka jhaag nahi bana, matlab sabun kharab hai\"**\n\nAksar sabun kharab nahi, **paani kathor** hota hai.\n\n**Galti 6: Activity ke paani ko peena ya chakhna**\n\nActivity 3.1 ke kisi bhi bottle ka paani **kabhi peena nahi**. Wo sabun mila hua hai, aur distilled paani bhi swaad ya sehat ke liye peene ka nahi hota.",
            "bodyHinglish": "**Galti 1: \"Kathor paani zeheela hota hai\"**\n\nNahi. Kathor paani mein calcium aur magnesium ke salt hote hain, jo aam taur par hanikarak nahi. Problem **sabun, kettle aur boiler** ki hai.\n\n**Galti 2: \"Ubalne se har tarah ka kathor paani mridu ho jaata hai\"**\n\nUbalne se **sirf asthayi** kathorta jaati hai. **Sthayi** kathorta (chloride aur sulphate wali) **nahi** jaati.\n\n**Galti 3: \"Kettle ka scale ek tarah ka zang ya mitti hai\"**\n\nNahi. Wo **CaCO₃** hai: Ca(HCO₃)₂ ke ubalne se bana thos. Zang loha par banta hai, ye alag cheez hai.\n\n**Galti 4: \"Washing soda paani ko bhaap bana deta hai\" ya \"sab ghula deta hai\"**\n\nWashing soda Ca²⁺ aur Mg²⁺ ko CaCO₃ aur MgCO₃ **thos** bana kar paani se **bahar** karta hai. Wo ghulte nahi, neeche baithte hain.\n\n**Galti 5: \"Sabun ka jhaag nahi bana, matlab sabun kharab hai\"**\n\nAksar sabun kharab nahi, **paani kathor** hota hai.\n\n**Galti 6: Activity ke paani ko peena ya chakhna**\n\nActivity 3.1 ke kisi bhi bottle ka paani **kabhi peena nahi**. Wo sabun mila hua hai, aur distilled paani bhi swaad ya sehat ke liye peene ka nahi hota."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Quick Recap",
            "headingHinglish": "Quick Recap",
            "body": "- **Mridu paani:** Ca aur Mg ke salt bahut kam; sabun aasani se jhaag deta hai. **Kathor paani:** Ca aur Mg ke salt zyada; sabun ka jhaag mushkil se banta hai.\n- Kathor paani mein sabun **scum** banata hai (calcium ya magnesium ka sabun, jo nahi ghulta), isliye sabun barbaad hota hai. **Detergent** scum nahi banata.\n- **Asthayi kathorta:** Ca(HCO₃)₂ aur Mg(HCO₃)₂ se. Ubalne se jaati hai: **Ca(HCO₃)₂ → CaCO₃ + H₂O + CO₂**. Yahi **kettle scale** hai.\n- **Sthayi kathorta:** chloride aur sulphate (CaCl₂, MgSO₄, CaSO₄) se. Ubalne se **nahi** jaati.\n- **Washing soda** dono hatata hai (double displacement + precipitate): **CaCl₂ + Na₂CO₃ → CaCO₃ + 2NaCl**, **MgSO₄ + Na₂CO₃ → MgCO₃ + Na₂SO₄**.\n- **Ion-exchange (resin ya zeolite):** Ca²⁺ aur Mg²⁺ ko Na⁺ se badalta hai. **Distillation** sabse shuddh, par mehnga.\n- Nuksan: sabun ki barbaadi, kettle aur geyser mein scale (bijli zyada), boiler aur pipe kharab, rangai mein dikkat. Fayde: thoda calcium aur magnesium milta hai, kuch logon ko swaad achha lagta hai.\n- Activity mein paani **kabhi peena nahi**; ubalne ka kaam adult karta hai.",
            "bodyHinglish": "- **Mridu paani:** Ca aur Mg ke salt bahut kam; sabun aasani se jhaag deta hai. **Kathor paani:** Ca aur Mg ke salt zyada; sabun ka jhaag mushkil se banta hai.\n- Kathor paani mein sabun **scum** banata hai (calcium ya magnesium ka sabun, jo nahi ghulta), isliye sabun barbaad hota hai. **Detergent** scum nahi banata.\n- **Asthayi kathorta:** Ca(HCO₃)₂ aur Mg(HCO₃)₂ se. Ubalne se jaati hai: **Ca(HCO₃)₂ → CaCO₃ + H₂O + CO₂**. Yahi **kettle scale** hai.\n- **Sthayi kathorta:** chloride aur sulphate (CaCl₂, MgSO₄, CaSO₄) se. Ubalne se **nahi** jaati.\n- **Washing soda** dono hatata hai (double displacement + precipitate): **CaCl₂ + Na₂CO₃ → CaCO₃ + 2NaCl**, **MgSO₄ + Na₂CO₃ → MgCO₃ + Na₂SO₄**.\n- **Ion-exchange (resin ya zeolite):** Ca²⁺ aur Mg²⁺ ko Na⁺ se badalta hai. **Distillation** sabse shuddh, par mehnga.\n- Nuksan: sabun ki barbaadi, kettle aur geyser mein scale (bijli zyada), boiler aur pipe kharab, rangai mein dikkat. Fayde: thoda calcium aur magnesium milta hai, kuch logon ko swaad achha lagta hai.\n- Activity mein paani **kabhi peena nahi**; ubalne ka kaam adult karta hai."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Practice Questions",
            "headingHinglish": "Practice Questions",
            "body": "1. What is the difference between hard water and soft water? Give one example of each.\n\n2. Why does soap not form a good lather in hard water? What is the white scum made of (in words)?\n\n3. Distinguish between temporary and permanent hardness in a table (cause, compounds, effect of boiling).\n\n4. Write the equation for what happens when magnesium hydrogencarbonate is boiled. Check that it is balanced, and say which product is the solid.\n\n5. 7.3 g of Mg(HCO₃)₂ in water is boiled completely. Find the mass of MgCO₃ formed. (Mg = 24, H = 1, C = 12, O = 16.)\n\n6. Hard water contains 2.4 g of MgSO₄. (a) Write the equation for removing it with washing soda. (b) Find the mass of Na₂CO₃ needed and the mass of MgCO₃ formed. (Mg = 24, S = 32, O = 16, Na = 23, C = 12.)\n\n7. A student boils a sample of tap water and then tests it with soap. The lather is the same as before boiling. What kind of hardness does the water have, and why?\n\n8. Explain why boiling does not remove the hardness caused by CaCl₂ but removes the hardness caused by Ca(HCO₃)₂.\n\n9. Name two ways of removing permanent hardness. Which one is used in home water softeners? Describe it in one or two lines.\n\n10. List three disadvantages of hard water in the home or in industry, and one benefit.\n\n11. A bucket of hard water is used in a factory boiler. Why is a thick scale a problem there? (Give two reasons.)\n\n12. State True or False and correct the false ones:\n    (a) Hard water is poisonous.\n    (b) Detergents form scum with hard water in the same way as soap.\n    (c) Kettle scale is mainly CaCO₃.\n    (d) Boiling removes both temporary and permanent hardness.\n    (e) Distilled water is soft.\n\n13. A student does the soap-lather activity with tap water, boiled-and-cooled tap water and distilled water. Which should give the most lather, and what safety rules must be followed?\n\n### Answers\n\n1. **Kathor paani** mein calcium aur magnesium ke salt **zyada** hote hain, sabun ka jhaag mushkil se banta hai (jaise kai borewell ya kuein ka paani). **Mridu paani** mein ye salt **bahut kam** hote hain, sabun aasani se jhaag deta hai (jaise baarish ka paani ya distilled paani).\n\n2. Sabun ka sodium wala hissa **Ca²⁺ ya Mg²⁺ se milkar** calcium ya magnesium ka sabun banata hai, jo **paani mein nahi ghulta**. Wahi **scum** hai: **calcium ya magnesium ka sabun**. Jab tak saare Ca²⁺ aur Mg²⁺ khatam nahi hote, sabun scum banane mein jaata rehta hai aur jhaag nahi banta.\n\n3. | Baat | Asthayi (temporary) | Sthayi (permanent) |\n   |---|---|---|\n   | Karan | Ca aur Mg ke hydrogencarbonate | Ca aur Mg ke chloride aur sulphate |\n   | Compounds | Ca(HCO₃)₂, Mg(HCO₃)₂ | CaCl₂, MgCl₂, CaSO₄, MgSO₄ |\n   | Ubalne ka asar | Kathorta **hat jaati** hai | Kathorta **nahi** hatti |\n\n4. **Mg(HCO₃)₂ → MgCO₃ + H₂O + CO₂.** Ginti: Mg 1=1, H 2=2, C 2=2 (1 + 1), O 6=6 (3 + 1 + 2) ✅. **MgCO₃** thos hai (paani mein nahi ghulta); H₂O paani, CO₂ gas.\n\n5. Mg(HCO₃)₂ = 24 + 2 × 61 = **146 u**. MgCO₃ = 24 + 12 + 48 = **84 u**. Check: 84 + 18 + 44 = 146 ✅. 146 g se 84 g MgCO₃. To 7.3 g se: 7.3 × 84 ÷ 146 = **4.2 g MgCO₃**. Jaanch: 7.3 ÷ 146 = 0.05, aur 0.05 × 84 = 4.2 ✅.\n\n6. (a) **MgSO₄ + Na₂CO₃ → MgCO₃ + Na₂SO₄.** Ginti: Mg 1=1, S 1=1, Na 2=2, C 1=1, O 7=7 ✅. (b) MgSO₄ = 24 + 32 + 64 = **120 u**; Na₂CO₃ = **106 u**; MgCO₃ = **84 u**; Na₂SO₄ = 46 + 32 + 64 = **142 u**. Mass check: 120 + 106 = 226 = 84 + 142 ✅. 2.4 g MgSO₄ ka matlab 2.4 ÷ 120 = 0.02. Na₂CO₃: 0.02 × 106 = **2.12 g**. MgCO₃: 0.02 × 84 = **1.68 g**.\n\n7. Jhaag **same** raha, matlab ubalne se kathorta **nahi** gayi, isliye paani mein **sthayi kathorta** hai (chloride ya sulphate wale salt), kyunki ye ubalne par nahi tootte. (Ya paani mridu hi tha, tab bhi jhaag pehle se achha hota.)\n\n8. **Ca(HCO₃)₂** garam karne par **tootkar** CaCO₃ (thos), H₂O aur CO₂ deta hai, isliye Ca²⁺ thos mein chala gaya aur paani mridu ho gaya. **CaCl₂** garam karne par **nahi tootta**: Ca²⁺ aur Cl⁻ ion ghol mein hi rehte hain, isliye kathorta wahin rehti hai.\n\n9. **Washing soda** aur **ion-exchange** (aur distillation). Home softener mein **ion-exchange** hota hai: paani ek resin ya zeolite se guzarta hai, jo **Ca²⁺ aur Mg²⁺ ko pakad leta hai** aur badle mein **Na⁺** chhodta hai (ek Ca²⁺ ke badle do Na⁺). Sodium ke salt scum nahi banate.\n\n10. Nuksan (koi teen): sabun zyada lagta hai, kapde par scum, kettle ya geyser mein scale (bijli zyada), boiler ya pipe mein scale se nuksan, rangai mein dikkat. Fayda: kuch calcium aur magnesium milta hai (ya kuch logon ko swaad achha lagta hai).\n\n11. (i) Scale **garmi ka kharab conductor** hai, isliye garmi paani tak theek se nahi pahunchti, **fuel zyada kharch** hota hai. (ii) Scale se **pipe tang ya band** ho jaate hain, aur boiler ki deewar bahut garam hokar **kharab ya khatarnak** ho sakti hai.\n\n12. (a) **False** ❌. Kathor paani zeheela nahi hai; wo sirf sabun aur boiler ke liye pareshani hai. (b) **False** ❌. Detergent kathor paani mein **scum nahi** banata. (c) **True** ✅. (d) **False** ❌. Ubalne se **sirf asthayi** kathorta jaati hai. (e) **True** ✅. Distillation mein ghule salt peeche reh jaate hain.\n\n13. **Distilled paani** mein sabse zyada jhaag (kyunki usme Ca²⁺ aur Mg²⁺ nahi). Ubala-thanda paani mein tap se zyada ho sakta hai, agar asthayi kathorta thi. Safety: **adult ke saath** karna; ubalne ka kaam **sirf adult**; paani poori tarah thanda hone par hi use karna; **kisi bhi bottle ka paani peena ya chakhna nahi**; kaam ke baad paani sink mein baha dena, haath dho lena aur bottles ko khane-peene ke liye dobara use na karna.\n\n---\n\nShabaash! Ab tum jaante ho ki **kathor paani** mein Ca aur Mg ke salt hote hain, ki kettle ki safed parat **CaCO₃** hai jo Ca(HCO₃)₂ ke ubalne se banti hai, aur ki **washing soda** ya **ion-exchange** se Ca²⁺ aur Mg²⁺ ko paani se bahar kiya ja sakta hai.\n\n**Aage kya?** Ek sawaal bacha hai: **neela tutiya** (CuSO₄·5H₂O) ke crystal sookhe aur thos dikhte hain, par unke andar **paani chhipa hai**, aur garam karne par ye safed ho jaate hain. Aur ek aur: washing soda ke crystal khule mein rakhne par **powder** kyun ban jaate hain, jabki kuch namak khule mein rakhne par **gil jaate** hain? Agle topic **\"Paani Aur Crystals: Hydrates, Efflorescence aur Deliquescence\"** mein hum dekhenge ki crystals ke andar paani kaise rehta hai, aur ek chhote silica gel ke packet ka raaz bhi khulega.",
            "bodyHinglish": "1. What is the difference between hard water and soft water? Give one example of each.\n\n2. Why does soap not form a good lather in hard water? What is the white scum made of (in words)?\n\n3. Distinguish between temporary and permanent hardness in a table (cause, compounds, effect of boiling).\n\n4. Write the equation for what happens when magnesium hydrogencarbonate is boiled. Check that it is balanced, and say which product is the solid.\n\n5. 7.3 g of Mg(HCO₃)₂ in water is boiled completely. Find the mass of MgCO₃ formed. (Mg = 24, H = 1, C = 12, O = 16.)\n\n6. Hard water contains 2.4 g of MgSO₄. (a) Write the equation for removing it with washing soda. (b) Find the mass of Na₂CO₃ needed and the mass of MgCO₃ formed. (Mg = 24, S = 32, O = 16, Na = 23, C = 12.)\n\n7. A student boils a sample of tap water and then tests it with soap. The lather is the same as before boiling. What kind of hardness does the water have, and why?\n\n8. Explain why boiling does not remove the hardness caused by CaCl₂ but removes the hardness caused by Ca(HCO₃)₂.\n\n9. Name two ways of removing permanent hardness. Which one is used in home water softeners? Describe it in one or two lines.\n\n10. List three disadvantages of hard water in the home or in industry, and one benefit.\n\n11. A bucket of hard water is used in a factory boiler. Why is a thick scale a problem there? (Give two reasons.)\n\n12. State True or False and correct the false ones:\n    (a) Hard water is poisonous.\n    (b) Detergents form scum with hard water in the same way as soap.\n    (c) Kettle scale is mainly CaCO₃.\n    (d) Boiling removes both temporary and permanent hardness.\n    (e) Distilled water is soft.\n\n13. A student does the soap-lather activity with tap water, boiled-and-cooled tap water and distilled water. Which should give the most lather, and what safety rules must be followed?\n\n### Answers\n\n1. **Kathor paani** mein calcium aur magnesium ke salt **zyada** hote hain, sabun ka jhaag mushkil se banta hai (jaise kai borewell ya kuein ka paani). **Mridu paani** mein ye salt **bahut kam** hote hain, sabun aasani se jhaag deta hai (jaise baarish ka paani ya distilled paani).\n\n2. Sabun ka sodium wala hissa **Ca²⁺ ya Mg²⁺ se milkar** calcium ya magnesium ka sabun banata hai, jo **paani mein nahi ghulta**. Wahi **scum** hai: **calcium ya magnesium ka sabun**. Jab tak saare Ca²⁺ aur Mg²⁺ khatam nahi hote, sabun scum banane mein jaata rehta hai aur jhaag nahi banta.\n\n3. | Baat | Asthayi (temporary) | Sthayi (permanent) |\n   |---|---|---|\n   | Karan | Ca aur Mg ke hydrogencarbonate | Ca aur Mg ke chloride aur sulphate |\n   | Compounds | Ca(HCO₃)₂, Mg(HCO₃)₂ | CaCl₂, MgCl₂, CaSO₄, MgSO₄ |\n   | Ubalne ka asar | Kathorta **hat jaati** hai | Kathorta **nahi** hatti |\n\n4. **Mg(HCO₃)₂ → MgCO₃ + H₂O + CO₂.** Ginti: Mg 1=1, H 2=2, C 2=2 (1 + 1), O 6=6 (3 + 1 + 2) ✅. **MgCO₃** thos hai (paani mein nahi ghulta); H₂O paani, CO₂ gas.\n\n5. Mg(HCO₃)₂ = 24 + 2 × 61 = **146 u**. MgCO₃ = 24 + 12 + 48 = **84 u**. Check: 84 + 18 + 44 = 146 ✅. 146 g se 84 g MgCO₃. To 7.3 g se: 7.3 × 84 ÷ 146 = **4.2 g MgCO₃**. Jaanch: 7.3 ÷ 146 = 0.05, aur 0.05 × 84 = 4.2 ✅.\n\n6. (a) **MgSO₄ + Na₂CO₃ → MgCO₃ + Na₂SO₄.** Ginti: Mg 1=1, S 1=1, Na 2=2, C 1=1, O 7=7 ✅. (b) MgSO₄ = 24 + 32 + 64 = **120 u**; Na₂CO₃ = **106 u**; MgCO₃ = **84 u**; Na₂SO₄ = 46 + 32 + 64 = **142 u**. Mass check: 120 + 106 = 226 = 84 + 142 ✅. 2.4 g MgSO₄ ka matlab 2.4 ÷ 120 = 0.02. Na₂CO₃: 0.02 × 106 = **2.12 g**. MgCO₃: 0.02 × 84 = **1.68 g**.\n\n7. Jhaag **same** raha, matlab ubalne se kathorta **nahi** gayi, isliye paani mein **sthayi kathorta** hai (chloride ya sulphate wale salt), kyunki ye ubalne par nahi tootte. (Ya paani mridu hi tha, tab bhi jhaag pehle se achha hota.)\n\n8. **Ca(HCO₃)₂** garam karne par **tootkar** CaCO₃ (thos), H₂O aur CO₂ deta hai, isliye Ca²⁺ thos mein chala gaya aur paani mridu ho gaya. **CaCl₂** garam karne par **nahi tootta**: Ca²⁺ aur Cl⁻ ion ghol mein hi rehte hain, isliye kathorta wahin rehti hai.\n\n9. **Washing soda** aur **ion-exchange** (aur distillation). Home softener mein **ion-exchange** hota hai: paani ek resin ya zeolite se guzarta hai, jo **Ca²⁺ aur Mg²⁺ ko pakad leta hai** aur badle mein **Na⁺** chhodta hai (ek Ca²⁺ ke badle do Na⁺). Sodium ke salt scum nahi banate.\n\n10. Nuksan (koi teen): sabun zyada lagta hai, kapde par scum, kettle ya geyser mein scale (bijli zyada), boiler ya pipe mein scale se nuksan, rangai mein dikkat. Fayda: kuch calcium aur magnesium milta hai (ya kuch logon ko swaad achha lagta hai).\n\n11. (i) Scale **garmi ka kharab conductor** hai, isliye garmi paani tak theek se nahi pahunchti, **fuel zyada kharch** hota hai. (ii) Scale se **pipe tang ya band** ho jaate hain, aur boiler ki deewar bahut garam hokar **kharab ya khatarnak** ho sakti hai.\n\n12. (a) **False** ❌. Kathor paani zeheela nahi hai; wo sirf sabun aur boiler ke liye pareshani hai. (b) **False** ❌. Detergent kathor paani mein **scum nahi** banata. (c) **True** ✅. (d) **False** ❌. Ubalne se **sirf asthayi** kathorta jaati hai. (e) **True** ✅. Distillation mein ghule salt peeche reh jaate hain.\n\n13. **Distilled paani** mein sabse zyada jhaag (kyunki usme Ca²⁺ aur Mg²⁺ nahi). Ubala-thanda paani mein tap se zyada ho sakta hai, agar asthayi kathorta thi. Safety: **adult ke saath** karna; ubalne ka kaam **sirf adult**; paani poori tarah thanda hone par hi use karna; **kisi bhi bottle ka paani peena ya chakhna nahi**; kaam ke baad paani sink mein baha dena, haath dho lena aur bottles ko khane-peene ke liye dobara use na karna.\n\n---\n\nShabaash! Ab tum jaante ho ki **kathor paani** mein Ca aur Mg ke salt hote hain, ki kettle ki safed parat **CaCO₃** hai jo Ca(HCO₃)₂ ke ubalne se banti hai, aur ki **washing soda** ya **ion-exchange** se Ca²⁺ aur Mg²⁺ ko paani se bahar kiya ja sakta hai.\n\n**Aage kya?** Ek sawaal bacha hai: **neela tutiya** (CuSO₄·5H₂O) ke crystal sookhe aur thos dikhte hain, par unke andar **paani chhipa hai**, aur garam karne par ye safed ho jaate hain. Aur ek aur: washing soda ke crystal khule mein rakhne par **powder** kyun ban jaate hain, jabki kuch namak khule mein rakhne par **gil jaate** hain? Agle topic **\"Paani Aur Crystals: Hydrates, Efflorescence aur Deliquescence\"** mein hum dekhenge ki crystals ke andar paani kaise rehta hai, aur ek chhote silica gel ke packet ka raaz bhi khulega."
          }
